'nyt://article/91409e2d-d436-5922-b2b6-9505f3c66967', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91409e2d-d436-5922-b2b6-9505f3c66967'}, {'abstract': '“Moby-Dick” contained the author’s diagnosis, prognosis and prescription for the human condition. We didn’t listen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/02/books/review/herman-melville-moby-dick.html', 'snippet': '“Moby-Dick” contained the author’s diagnosis, prognosis and prescription for the human condition. We didn’t listen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1841, while aboard the whaler Acushnet, Herman Melville met William Chase among another ship’s complement. William lent Melville a book by his father, Owen Chase: “Narrative of the Most Extraordinary and Distressing Shipwreck of the Whale-Ship Essex.” Melville had read Jeremiah Reynolds’s violent account of a sperm whale “white as wool,” named — for his haunt near Mocha Island, off the coast of Chile — Mocha Dick. It’s unknown what led Melville to tweak Mocha to “Moby.” Good thing he did, and that Starbuck was the name he gave his first mate rather than his captain. Otherwise the novel would follow Starbuck’s obsession with a Mocha.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/14/books/review/00Safina/00Safina-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/14/books/review/00Safina/00Safina-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/14/books/review/00Safina/00Safina-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/14/books/review/00Safina/00Safina-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/14/books/review/00Safina/00Safina-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/06/14/books/review/00Safina/00Safina-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/14/books/review/00Safina/00Safina-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Melville’s Whale Was a Warning We Failed to Heed', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Moby-Dick (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Melville, Herman', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-02T09:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Safina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Safina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcf3823c-3871-51be-b7df-c03a73d789a9', 'word_count': 1405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcf3823c-3871-51be-b7df-c03a73d789a9'}, {'abstract': 'A former city reporter went to the Middle East, looking for the big story. Now she yearns for the city she thought she was happy to leave behind.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/02/nyregion/coronavirus-missing-nyc.html', 'snippet': 'A former city reporter went to the Middle East, looking for the big story. Now she yearns for the city she thought she was happy to leave behind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I live in Beirut, Lebanon, but in this season of confinement I could be anywhere. I have left my apartment eight times in six weeks; my brushes with the city where I’ve lived for a year and a half are so brief, I forgot that I lived near the sea until I went up on a roof and my eyes confronted the blue fact of the Mediterranean. In my apartment, with friends nine time zones away as accessible as friends down the block, I Zoom far and wide. I could be anywhere, but some part of me wants to be in New York.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/03/nyregion/03missingcity-houston/merlin_171715461_f8816db7-4b79-477b-93ed-21c7e3469f25-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/03/nyregion/03missingcity-houston/merlin_171715461_f8816db7-4b79-477b-93ed-21c7e3469f25-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/03/nyregion/03missingcity-houston/merlin_171715461_f8816db7-4b79-477b-93ed-21c7e3469f25-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/03/nyregion/03missingcity-houston/merlin_171715461_f8816db7-4b79-477b-93ed-21c7e3469f25-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/03/nyregion/03missingcity-houston/merlin_171715461_f8816db7-4b79-477b-93ed-21c7e3469f25-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/03/nyregion/03missingcity-houston/merlin_171715461_f8816db7-4b79-477b-93ed-21c7e3469f25-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/03/nyregion/03missingcity-houston/merlin_171715461_f8816db7-4b79-477b-93ed-21c7e3469f25-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Is Wounded. I Miss It More Than Ever.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Longing for the Strangers of New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beirut (Lebanon)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-02T09:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian Yee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c4c295e-f1b6-5621-aad6-fa710b09f5e5', 'word_count': 1235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c4c295e-f1b6-5621-aad6-fa710b09f5e5'}, {'abstract': 'New Yorkers with no better place to go keep riding and sleeping on otherwise empty trains, stirring public health fears and prompting a nightly shutdown for cleaning.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/02/nyregion/coronavirus-nyc-subway-homeless.html', 'snippet': 'New Yorkers with no better place to go keep riding and sleeping on otherwise empty trains, stirring public health fears and prompting a nightly shutdown for cleaning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every No. 2 train that lumbered into the last stop in the Bronx late Wednesday night had, at most, a couple of dozen passengers. And when the doors swooshed open, half of them had no intention of getting off.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/01/nyregion/01nyvirus-homeless/01nyvirus-homeless-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/01/nyregion/01nyvirus-homeless/01nyvirus-homeless-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/01/nyregion/01nyvirus-homeless/01nyvirus-homeless-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/01/nyregion/01nyvirus-homeless/01nyvirus-homeless-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/01/nyregion/01nyvirus-homeless/01nyvirus-homeless-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/01/nyregion/01nyvirus-homeless/01nyvirus-homeless-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/01/nyregion/01nyvirus-homeless/01nyvirus-homeless-thumbLarge.jp