'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buskirk', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4b17622-afce-5abc-afb9-ece75024362e', 'word_count': 954, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4b17622-afce-5abc-afb9-ece75024362e'}, {'abstract': 'After weeks spent indoors, people ventured outside in droves. But worried officials warned them to wear masks and keep social distance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/02/nyregion/weather-parks-nyc-nj-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'After weeks spent indoors, people ventured outside in droves. But worried officials warned them to wear masks and keep social distance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the second day of May, New Yorkers were greeted with sunny skies and the warmest weekend so far this spring. People got up off their couch, put on their shoes, donned their face coverings, and left their cramped houses and apartments for the nearest park — desperate for fresh air and a little exercise.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/02/nyregion/02nyvirus-parks-02/merlin_172133154_dfc0d666-8a3c-445b-a447-4dea926031b3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/02/nyregion/02nyvirus-parks-02/merlin_172133154_dfc0d666-8a3c-445b-a447-4dea926031b3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/02/nyregion/02nyvirus-parks-02/merlin_172133154_dfc0d666-8a3c-445b-a447-4dea926031b3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/02/nyregion/02nyvirus-parks-02/