erson': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruenig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0583f62d-570d-50fd-acbd-7d0b78c50aaf', 'word_count': 986, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0583f62d-570d-50fd-acbd-7d0b78c50aaf'}, {'abstract': 'For now, my future and that of other immigrants in America remains uncertain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/03/opinion/coronavirus-doctors-immigration-trump.html', 'snippet': 'For now, my future and that of other immigrants in America remains uncertain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — On April 20, I had just gotten home from a particularly difficult 14-hour shift when I saw President Trump’s tweet about closing the United States border to immigrants. He said that he was acting as a response to the coronavirus pandemic and to protect the jobs of American citizens. This was alarming news to me, especially since some of the reporting on the announcement suggested that visas for highly skilled workers could also be banned. As a foreign-born doctor on a work visa, I was very worried about how this would impact my ability to remain in the country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/01/opinion/01Faraz2/01Faraz2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/01/opinion/01Faraz2/01Faraz2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/01/opinion/01Faraz2/01Faraz2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/01/opinion/01Faraz2/01Faraz2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/01/opinion/01Faraz2/01Faraz2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/01/opinion/01Faraz2/01Faraz2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/01/opinion/01Faraz2/01Faraz2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'President Trump, I Am Not Your Enemy. I Am a Doctor.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Workers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Orders and Memorandums', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-03T19:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shahdabul Faraz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shahdabul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Faraz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c287e29-da86-5b2e-8b21-32717220ba3c', 'word_count': 890, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c287e29-da86-5b2e-8b21-32717220ba3c'}, {'abstract': 'Here’s one idea for protecting them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/03/opinion/coronavirus-nursing-homes.html', 'snippet': 'Here’s one idea for protecting them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRISTOL, Conn. — My family has owned an assisted living home in this town for over 44 years. Both of my grandmothers have lived in it, and my mother might soon need its care. As much as I admired my parents, I did not think I would someday lead it. I went to Yale, served three tours in Iraq as a Marine infantry officer and earned a Ph.D. in political science from Harvard. I had planned to turn my dissertation into a book.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/03/opinion/03beg4/merlin_172096590_6aae5839-2343-4a9d-88e4-daa5909355c6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/03/opinion/03beg4/merlin_172096590_6aae5839-2343-4a9d-88e4-daa5909355c6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/03/opinion/03beg4/merlin_172096590_6aae5839-2343-4a9d-88e4-daa5909355c6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/03/opinion/03beg4/merlin_172096590_6aae5839-2343-4a9d-88e4-daa5909355c6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/03/opinion/03beg4/merlin_172096590_6aae5839-2343-4a9d-88e4-daa5909355c6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subTyp