to plan for global partnership to recover.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hard to imagine that 97 percent of Americans could agree on anything right now. But that is how many told Pew Research they either strongly (86 percent) or somewhat (11 percent) support international cooperation to fight infectious disease.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/04/opinion/04hurlburt/04hurlburt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/04/opinion/04hurlburt/04hurlburt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 500}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/04/opinion/04hurlburt/04hurlburt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 853, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/04/opinion/04hurlburt/04hurlburt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1707, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/04/opinion/04hurlburt/04hurlburt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/04/opinion/04hurlburt/04hurlburt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/04/opinion/04hurlburt/04hurlburt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The World Is Helping Americans Who Don’t Always See It', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Enterprise Institute for Public Policy Research', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-04T19:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Heather Hurlburt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hurlburt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1ccef53-0d89-52ac-8250-c52a05da7b57', 'word_count': 1121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1ccef53-0d89-52ac-8250-c52a05da7b57'}, {'abstract': 'Funding food banks while not expanding food stamps is a solution driven by ideology rather than effectiveness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/04/opinion/coronavirus-food-stamps.html', 'snippet': 'Funding food banks while not expanding food stamps is a solution driven by ideology rather than effectiveness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans are lined up dozens, hundreds and sometimes thousands deep at food pantries across the nation. One in every six Americans has lost their job in the pandemic, and the number will likely grow much larger before we start adding jobs again. Since March when business shutdowns began to prevent exposure to Covid-19, 1.9 million Texans have filed applications for benefits. That’s more than double all the claims submitted in the state in the entire year of 2019. In Iowa, more people filed for unemployment in March than in all of 2019.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/05/opinion/01Leonard-Russell-Beto1/merlin_165483033_2cf97ef6-59c7-4079-a35d-955572484335-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/05/opinion/01Leonard-Russell-Beto1/merlin_165483033_2cf97ef6-59c7-4079-a35d-955572484335-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/05/opinion/01Leonard-Russell-Beto1/merlin_165483033_2cf97ef6-59c7-4079-a35d-955572484335-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/05/opinion/01Leonard-Russell-Beto1/merlin_165483033_2cf97ef6-59c7-4079-a35d-955572484335-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/05/opinion/01Leonard-Russell-Beto1/01Leonard-Russell-Beto1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/05/opinion/01Leonard-Russell-Beto1/01Leonard-Russell-Beto1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/05/opinion/01Leonard-Russell-Beto1/01Leonard-Russell-Beto1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Americans Are Lining Up for Food. What Is Team Trump Doing?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Feed Americans Quickly', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Banks and Pantries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Aid', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Stamps', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE DEPARTMENT', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perdue, Sonny', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-04T19:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': "By Matt Russell, Robert Leonard and Beto O'Rourke", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Russell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Beto', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Rourke", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/13920fe9-bc35-58df-83c2-5dc24559dfcb', 'word_count': 1245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13920fe9-bc35-58df-83c2-5dc24559dfcb'}, {'abstract': 'As Italians move toward a less stringent regimen to minimize their exposure to the coronavirus, they can take pride in an unusual collective effort.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/04/opinion/italy-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'As Italians move toward a less stringent regimen to minimize their exposure to the coronavirus, they can take pride in an unusual collective effort.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CREMA, Italy — The first country outside Asia to experience the coronavirus pandemic on a large scale was Italy. It was the first to go into lockdown and impose a national quarantine, on March 9. And it is the part of Europe that suffered most. As of May 3, 29,000 people were known to have lost their lives because of Covid-19. The actual figures are likely to be higher, as they will be everywhere else. My northern region — Lombardy, Italy’s economic powerhouse — has registered half of the country’s deaths. Army truck convoys carried coffins to crematories around the country from Bergamo — where the death rate in March and April rose to more than four times what it was last year. Brescia, Lodi, Cremona and Crema — where I live — were also deeply affected. My hometown has been a ghost town for two months. People moaned but stayed at home.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/05/opinion/05Severgnini1/merlin_171927039_039f43e5-b8a7-4ddc-bc1b-2da2e6e493d9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/05/opinion/05Severgnini1/merlin_171927039_039f43e5-b8a7-4ddc-bc1b-2da2e6e493d9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/05/opinion/05Severgnini1/merlin_171927039_039f43e5-b8a7-4ddc-bc1b-2da2e6e493d9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image