pe': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/04/world/04virus-fundraising/04virus-fundraising-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'World Leaders Join to Pledge $8 Billion for Vaccine as U.S. Goes It Alone', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Nations Steer Billions  To Vaccine, U.S. Sits Out', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gates, Bill and Melinda, Foundation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-04T22:26:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matina Stevis-Gridneff and Lara Jakes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stevis-Gridneff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Lara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jakes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccde815f-e751-5602-9803-b9795de6176d', 'word_count': 1122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccde815f-e751-5602-9803-b9795de6176d'}, {'abstract': 'Commander’s Palace in New Orleans now ships meals for two or four nationwide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/04/dining/commanders-palace-new-orleans.html', 'snippet': 'Commander’s Palace in New Orleans now ships meals for two or four nationwide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You’ll need to assemble your own jazz band or find a playlist on Spotify to do justice to a Commander’s Palace dinner at home, especially for Mother’s Day. For the first time, the legendary New Orleans restaurant, in business since 1893, is serving a limited menu for delivery, shipped frozen and nationwide through Goldbelly. The menu offers a three-course dinner for two ($179) or four ($299), with turtle soup, garlic bread, sweet and spicy quail, and pecan pie. À la carte options, serving two or four, are also available. Though the soup just takes a reheat once it’s thawed, for the quail you’ll have to channel your inner Paul Prudhomme and Emeril Lagasse — the birds come raw with the ingredients and instructions for stuffing, glazing and roasting them. All the items in the package can be refrigerated for a couple of days, so you have wiggle room in terms of timing. They send an entire pecan pie regardless of the order. There is a limited number of orders filled each day, and delivery is usually about two days from when the order is placed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/04/dining/04CommandersPalace1/04CommandersPalace1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 546, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/04/dining/04CommandersPalace1/04CommandersPalace1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 546}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/04/dining/04CommandersPalace1/04CommandersPalace1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 932, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/04/dining/04CommandersPalace1/04CommandersPalace1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1131, 'width': 1242, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/04/dining/04CommandersPalace1/04CommandersPalace1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/04/dining/04CommandersPalace1/04CommandersPalace1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/04/dining/04CommandersPalace1/04CommandersPalace1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Be a New Orleanian Wherever You Are', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mail Order Companies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Commander's Palace (New Orleans, La, Restaurant)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldbelly Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poultry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-04T22:31:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1adece5d-d4f1-5da6-9d42-8cbff4b59bf6', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1adece5d-d4f1-5da6-9d42-8cbff4b59bf6'}, {'abstract': 'The Chef’s Garden in Ohio has opened its vegetable sales to home cooks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/04/dining/the-chefs-garden-produce-delivery.html', 'snippet': 'The Chef’s Garden in Ohio has opened its vegetable sales to home cooks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For decades, the Chef’s Garden, a 350-acre farm in Huron, Ohio, has been a source of first-rate produce for restaurants across the country. Now the hundreds of items it cultivates are available for home delivery. What makes the offerings so compelling to the discerning cook is not just the dazzling seasonal variety — including sultry purple asparagus, glossy little squashes and bundles of frilly braising greens — but its utter freshness. And when it comes to some items like lettuces, just-picked freshness makes a huge difference. The vegetables look and taste better and even last longer in your fridge. There are assorted produce boxes containing the farm’s choices starting at $59, or you can assemble your own item by item.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/06/dining/04burner-garden/04burner-garden-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/06/dining/04burner-garden/04burner-garden-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/06/dining/04burner-garden/04burner-garden-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/06/dinin