oks and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Everett, Percival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Telephone (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-05T09:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rivka Galchen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rivka', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galchen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ce66bfc-71de-5ff1-b8a9-1d70dfc5fd38', 'word_count': 761, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ce66bfc-71de-5ff1-b8a9-1d70dfc5fd38'}, {'abstract': 'Telemedicine is teaching us new ways to communicate with our patients.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/05/well/live/doctors-patients-mother-baby-pediatrics-telemedicine-computers.html', 'snippet': 'Telemedicine is teaching us new ways to communicate with our patients.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I wait for the interpreter to call the mother and then connect me into our three-way call, I berate myself for how bad my Spanish has become. I imagine it will continue to get worse. But what I am also realizing in this 30 seconds of dead airtime is that my overall communication skills are dwindling, too. I realize that in normal, non-Covid times, I do a lot of nonverbal communication with my patients. That I can’t do over the telephone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/29/well/well-doctors-telehealth/well-doctors-telehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/04/29/well/well-doctors-telehealth/well-doctors-telehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0,