: 'Masks', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-05T09:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Live', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marjorie S. Rosenthal, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marjorie', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12dc5ffa-92c3-561c-9005-d24b7dca04f4', 'word_count': 1041, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12dc5ffa-92c3-561c-9005-d24b7dca04f4'}, {'abstract': 'With the world effectively on pause, now is a unique opportunity to listen to those close to you, or to those you wish were closer to you.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/05/well/family/listening-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'With the world effectively on pause, now is a unique opportunity to listen to those close to you, or to those you wish were closer to you.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Crises have a way of shining a klieg light on the quality and depth of one’s relationships. Following major hurricanes, severe winter storms, electrical outages and terrorist attacks such as 9/11, there tends to be an uptick in divorces and breakups, as well as marriages and pregnancies. Lawyers and demographers are already predicting a wave of Covid-divorces and coronababies as the pandemic has the potential to both bring us together and drive us apart.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/03/smarter-living/00well-listening-pandemic/00well-listening-pandemic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/03/smarter-living/00well-listening-pandemic/00well-listening-