eccentric and personal.” Lesser isn’t here to win converts, but even those unmoved by its subject will thrill to the book, a beautifully crafted inquiry into fiction, reality, crime and place.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/02/books/review/05Tuttle/05Tuttle-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 664, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/08/02/books/review/05Tuttle/05Tuttle-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 664}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/02/books/review/05Tuttle/05Tuttle-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/02/books/review/05Tuttle/05Tuttle-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1850, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/02/books/review/05Tuttle/05Tuttle-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/08/02/books/review/05Tuttle/05Tuttle-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/08/02/books/review/05Tuttle/05Tuttle-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Decades of Reading Scandinavian Crime Fiction Can Teach You', 'kicker': 'Nonfiction', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Crime and Place', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lesser, Wendy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Scandinavian Noir: In Pursuit of a Mystery (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scandinavia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-05T09:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Tuttle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tuttle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/72f7a306-e928-542b-983c-7e78a51532b3', 'word_count': 702, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72f7a306-e928-542b-983c-7e78a51532b3'}, {'abstract': 'Time and time again, baseball has helped our country recover and come together in times of loss. It can help us during the pandemic, too.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/05/opinion/scott-boras-mlb-baseball-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'Time and time again, baseball has helped our country recover and come together in times of loss. It can help us during the pandemic, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In some of America’s darkest moments, the country has turned to Major League Baseball to bring hope and normalcy back to everyday life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/05/opinion/05Boras/05Boras-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/05/opinion/05Boras/05Boras-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption