_paragraph': 'In March, as a wave of states began delaying their spring primaries because of the coronavirus, Wisconsin’s election, scheduled for April 7, loomed. The ballot for that day included the presidential primary, thousands of local offices and four judgeships, including a key seat on the Wisconsin Supreme Court. On March 17, the day after Ohio postponed its spring election, voting rights groups asked Wisconsin’s Democratic governor, Tony Evers, to do the same. “No one wanted the election to happen more than us, but it felt like this wave was about to hit our communities,” Angela Lang, the founder and executive director of the Milwaukee group Black Leaders Organizing for Community, a nonprofit organization, told me.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/magazine/10mag-Voting-image1/10mag-Voting-image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/10/magazine/10mag-Voting-image1/10mag-Voting-image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 438}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/magazine/10mag-Voting-image1/10mag-Voting-image1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 748, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/magazine/10mag-Voting-image1/10mag-Voting-image1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1495, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/magazine/10mag-Voting-image1/10mag-Voting-image1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/10/magazine/10mag-Voting-image1/10mag-Voting-image1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/magazine/10mag-Voting-image1/10mag-Voting-image1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Will Americans Lose Their Right to Vote in the Pandemic?', 'kicker': 'Feature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Can Democracy Survive the Pandemic?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Absentee Voting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-05T09:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Bazelon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bazelon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce720168-11f5-587f-99b1-9e213cd32ebd', 'word_count': 6453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce720168-11f5-587f-99b1-9e213cd32ebd'}, {'abstract': 'In concert with other free nations, America must restore its economic sovereignty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/05/opinion/hawley-abolish-wto-china.html', 'snippet': 'In concert with other free nations, America must restore its economic sovereignty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The coronavirus emergency is not only a public health crisis. With 30 million Americans unemployed, it is also an economic crisis. And it has exposed a hard truth about the modern global economy: it weakens American workers and has empowered China’s rise. That must change.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/05/opinion/05hawley2/05hawley2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/05/opinion/05hawley2/05hawley2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/05/opinion/05hawley2/05hawley2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/05/opinion/05hawley2/05hawley2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1349, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/05/opinion/05hawley2/05hawley2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/05/opinion/05hawley2/05hawley2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/05/opinion/05hawley2/05hawley2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The W.T.O. Should Be Abolished', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Abolish The W.T.O.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-05T09:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Hawley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hawley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/412a3394-36fb-5b12-8d78-a96b75865cff', 'word_count': 842, 'uri': 'nyt://article/412a3394-36fb-5b12-8d78-a96b75865cff'}, {'abstract': 'Joel Prouty is in high demand during the pandemic, a time when dancers, especially, need to get their sweat on.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/05/arts/dance/joel-prouty-cross-trainer-ballet.html', 'snippet': 'Joel Prouty is in high demand during the pandemic, a time when dancers, especially, need to get their sweat on.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bodies run on different engines and as far as exercise goes, dancers needs premium fuel. You can’t just take a ballerina and tell her do a squat. A squat needs a reason behind it. “So let’s take that reason and add to it,” said the personal trainer Joel Prouty. “Let’s make it vulnerable, let’s make it meaningful, let’s make it add to what that client is doing in a season.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/arts/10prouty-1/merlin_171992763_0a5c3951-140f-4168-9689-a175c4d10d98-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/10/arts/10prouty-1/merlin_171992763_0a5c3951-140f-4168-9689-a175c4d10d98-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/arts/10prouty-1/merlin_171992763_0a5c3951-140f-4168-9689-a175c4d10d98-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/arts/10prouty-1/merlin_171992763_0a5c3951-140f-4168-9689-a175c4d10d98-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/arts/10prouty-1/merlin_171992763_0a5c3951-140f-4168-9689-a175c4d10d98-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/10/arts/10prouty-1/merlin_171992763_0a5c3951-140f-4168-9689-a175c4d10d98-thumbStandard.jp