ern side of the town roundabout, Astrid knew that her life had changed, the shock of which was indistinguishable from relief. It was already a busy day—she’d spent the morning in the garden, she had a haircut appointment at 11:30, and then her granddaughter, Cecelia, was arriving by train with two suitcases and zero parents (no school bus accidents there—just a needed escape hatch), and Astrid was to meet her at the Clapham station to bring her back to the Big House.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘All Adults Here,’ by Emma Straub: An Excerpt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-05-05T09:01:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c8fb8cd-09b0-58a7-92ec-3fb92769a168', 'word_count': 2025, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c8fb8cd-09b0-58a7-92ec-3fb92769a168'}, {'abstract': 'An excerpt from “Little Eyes,” by Samanta Schweblin', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/05/books/review/little-eyes-by-samanta-schweblin-an-excerpt.html', 'snippet': 'An excerpt from “Little Eyes,” by Samanta Schweblin', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cheng shi‑xu had bought a kentuki card and established a connection with a device in Lyon. Since then, he’d spent over ten hours a day at his computer. His bank account balance was shrinking every day, his friends almost never called anymore, and all the fast food was burning a hole in his stomach. “So this is how you’re going to let yourself die?” his mother asked him over the phone, perhaps because she really had been working on her own death for years now, though he was always too busy to notice. For over a month now, though, Cheng Shi-Xu had been focused on something new: he was experiencing the birth of a great love, perhaps the most authentic and inexplicable of his life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Little Eyes,’ by Samanta Schweblin: An Excerpt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-05-05T09:01:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/819e86bd-1b23-5aa4-90da-4f4ffe94a591', 'word_count': 2897, 'uri': 'nyt://article/819e86bd-1b23-5aa4-90da-4f4ffe94a591'}, {'abstract': 'An excerpt from “Pelosi,” by Molly Ball', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/05/books/review/pelosi-by-molly-ball-an-excerpt.html', 'snippet': 'An excerpt from “Pelosi,” by Molly Ball', 'lead_paragraph': 'From an early age, Nancy D’Alesandro realized her mother never had much chance to be a person.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Pelosi,’ by Molly Ball: An Excerpt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-05-05T09:01:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2f06690-11ac-55a2-a2f8-f2d12b0c762e', 'word_count': 3589, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2f06690-11ac-55a2-a2f8-f2d12b0c762e'}, {'abstract': 'Jared Kushner tried to address a looming supply shortage with volunteers from the private sector. More than 1,000 people have died each day for over a month. Meat is growing scarcer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/05/us/coronavirus-live-news.html', 'snippet': 'Jared Kushner tried to address a looming supply shortage with volunteers from the private sector. More than 1,000 people have died each day for over a month. Meat is growing scarcer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This briefing has ended. Follow our latest coverage of the coronavirus pandemic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump Says Task Force Will Wind Down', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-05T09:16:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bf09413-3bad-5c67-88c6-b8e09873c747', 'word_count': 6532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bf09413-3bad-5c67-88c6-b8e09873c747'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo listed seven requirements that each of\xa0the state’s 10 regions\xa0must meet before restrictions could be eased.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/05/nyregion/coronavirus-nyc.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo listed seven requirements that each of\xa0the state’s 10 regions\xa0must meet before restrictions could be eased.', 'lead_paragraph': ' [Want to get New York Today by email? Here’s the sign-up.]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/05/nyregion/05nytoday/merlin_172037817_43439542-c424-40b5-9bd1-695b605661f8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/05/nyregion/05nytoday/merlin_172037817_43439542-c424-40b5-9bd1-695b605661f8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/05/nyregion/05nytoday/merlin_172037817_43439542-c424-40b5-9b