e-feldstein-favorites.html', 'snippet': 'The “Booksmart” actress, who plays a British rock critic in her new film, “How to Build a Girl,” also can’t live without “Gilmore Girls” and Stephen Sondheim.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In her new film, “How to Build a Girl,” (available in some drive-in theaters and on demand May 8), Beanie Feldstein plays a high school student in Wolverhampton, England, who makes a name for herself as a rock critic during the 1990s by writing virulently negative reviews of bands. It’s a stretch for the actress in more ways than one.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/arts/10my10-FeldsteinSUB/10my10-FeldsteinSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/10/arts/10my10-FeldsteinSUB/10my10-FeldsteinSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/arts/10my10-FeldsteinSUB/10my10-FeldsteinSUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 675, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/arts/10my10-FeldsteinSUB/10my10-FeldsteinSUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 675, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/arts/10my10-FeldsteinSUB/10my10-FeldsteinSUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/10/arts/10my10-FeldsteinSUB/10my10-FeldsteinSUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subt