'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Kelly and Peter Eavis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kelly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eavis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa7f5c6c-e495-5b40-bd47-141c746b41db', 'word_count': 1274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa7f5c6c-e495-5b40-bd47-141c746b41db'}, {'abstract': 'As head of an industry group, he fought Big Pharma to make treatments for AIDS and other diseases more affordable. And that was just one hat he wore.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/05/nyregion/william-haddad-dead.html', 'snippet': 'As head of an industry group, he fought Big Pharma to make treatments for AIDS and other diseases more affordable. And that was just one hat he wore.', 'lead_paragraph': 'William Haddad, a civic evangelist who helped streamline the sale of cheaper generic drugs to American consumers and pare the price of AIDS treatment globally to a dollar a day, died on April 30 at his home in Poughquag, N.Y., in the Hudson Valley. He was 91.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/06/obituaries/04Haddad1/merlin_172176267_57aa40f9-4e6a-446e-a0a7-eabed8fbfe69-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 423, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/06/obituaries/04Haddad1/merlin_172176267_57aa40f9-4e6a-446e-a0a7-eabed8fbfe69-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 423}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/06/obituaries/04Haddad1/merlin_172176267_57aa40f9-4e6a-446e-