section_name': 'Parenting', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/0893dc7f-9821-503a-8a9f-ba8577e93937', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/0893dc7f-9821-503a-8a9f-ba8577e93937'}, {'abstract': 'I had to find new ways to compartmentalize my depression and process my emotions without denying my mental health needs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/05/parenting/motherhood-depression.html', 'snippet': 'I had to find new ways to compartmentalize my depression and process my emotions without denying my mental health needs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m watching my toddler as she plays with her toys, and I feel nothing. I’m not sad or happy. I’m just there. She hands me the book du jour, “Tickle Time,” and signals for me to read it. I freeze, filled with dread. The hardest thing about reading “Tickle Time” isn’t the silly voice I have to adopt, or the ginned up enthusiasm or even the pièce de résistance: the tickling. It’s the fact that I want to do all these things, but my mind makes me feel like I can’t. Thankfully, by now I’m well-versed at performative happiness. My brain uses an emergency generator that powers the backup mom memory, which allows me to appear human and somewhat entertaining to my child. I am a Westworld mom, only lazier and less homicidal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/04/multimedia/04parenting-depression-top/04parenting-depression-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/04/multimedia/04parenting-depression-top/04parenting-depression-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/04/multimedia/04parenting-depression-top/04parenting-depression-top-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/04/multimedia/04parenting-depression-top/04parenting-depression-top-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 1600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/04/multimedia/04parenting-depression-top/04parenting-depression-top-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/04/multimedia/04parenting-depression-top/04parenting-depression-top-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/04/multimedia/04parenting-depression-top/04parenting-depression-top-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Becoming a New Mom With ‘Old Depression’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Depression (Mental)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-05T19:44:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Parenting', 'section_name': 'Parenting', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amanda Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/349ce914-a89f-5c82-9495-7315083d9112', 'word_count': 1179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/349ce914-a89f-5c82-9495-7315083d9112'}, {'abstract': 'How to shift your mind-set from giving so much of yourself to others.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/05/parenting/mothers-not-martyrs.html', 'snippet': 'How to shift your mind-set from giving so much of yourself to others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was teaching a group of new mothers a few years ago how to recognize postpartum depression and anxiety when a woman raised her hand. “My work is letting me take an extra two weeks of paid maternity leave. I don’t know what to do. I feel bad if I take it. My team will have to pick up the slack. I feel bad if I don’t. I’d be giving up precious time with my daughter.” I responded, “Is there any option you wouldn’t feel bad about taking?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/29/multimedia/29parenting-motherasmartyr/29parenting-motherasmartyr-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/04/29/multimedia/29parenting-motherasmartyr/29parenting-motherasmartyr-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/29/multimedia/29parenting-motherasmartyr/29parenting-motherasmartyr-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/29/multimedia/29parenting-motherasmartyr/29parenting-motherasmartyr-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1750, 'width': 1750, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/29/multimedia/29parenting-motherasmartyr/29parenting-motherasmartyr-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/04/29/multimedia/29parenting-motherasmartyr/29parenting-motherasmartyr-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/29/multimedia/29parenting-motherasmartyr/29parenting-motherasmartyr-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mothers Don’t Have to Be Martyrs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-05T19:45:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Parenting', 'section_name': 'Parenting', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pooja Lakshmin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pooja', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lakshmin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b5d406a-5101-597c-8ae4-b447beb4af17', 'word_count': 1375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b5d406a-5101-597c-8ae4-b447beb4af17'}, {'abstract': 'My husband and I gave her names that honor our heritage, but now we wonder if it’s enough.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/05/parenting/baby-name-family-history.html', 'snippet': 'My husband and I gave her names that honor our heritage, but now we wonder if it’s enough.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the longest time, when we said her name, our daughter wouldn’t turn her head. Though it was only one of several milestones that our now-toddler was behind on, this especially worried me. “Why doesn’t she know her name yet?” I would vent to my husband after another failed experiment, calling into the abyss. Finally, in one of our bedtime recaps of the day’s events — events meaning what our daughter did and when she did it — I asked my husband my real concern, “When will she know who she is?”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/fashion/5parenting-name-identity/5parenting-name-identity-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/10/fashion/5parenting-name-identity/5parenting-name-identity-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/fashion/5parenting-name-identity/5parenting-name-identity-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/fashion/5parenting-name-identity/5parenting-name-identity-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/fashion/5parenting-name-identity/5parenting-name-identity-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/10/fashion/5parenting-name-id