: None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c61f4c6d-245a-5e37-87dd-6d7a4296a0b5', 'word_count': 533, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c61f4c6d-245a-5e37-87dd-6d7a4296a0b5'}, {'abstract': 'A survey suggests that pandemic-era domestic work isn’t being divided more equitably than before the lockdown.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/06/upshot/pandemic-chores-homeschooling-gender.html', 'snippet': 'A survey suggests that pandemic-era domestic work isn’t being divided more equitably than before the lockdown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Home schooling, the new parental chore brought about by coronavirus lockdowns, is being handled disproportionately by women, according to a new poll by Morning Consult for The New York Times. Fathers don’t necessarily agree — nearly half of those with children under 12 report spending more time on it than their spouse — but just 3 percent of women say their spouse is doing more. Eighty percent of mothers say they spend more time on it.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/06/upshot/06up-virus-gender/merlin_171093174_613184b4-3756-4367-b3d4-53af7e56f5cc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/06/upshot/06up-virus-gender/merlin_171093174_613184b4-3756-4367-b3d4-53af7e56f5cc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/06/upshot/06up-virus-gender/merlin_171093174_613184b4-3756-4367-b3d4-53af7e56f5cc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'c