 'nyt://article/ad0a4bc6-8737-5093-9a45-1ef8938e77c1', 'word_count': 1426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad0a4bc6-8737-5093-9a45-1ef8938e77c1'}, {'abstract': 'Blue Flame Medical boasted that it could acquire masks, testing kits and other equipment to respond to the pandemic. State and local governments paid up — and are still waiting for delivery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/06/us/politics/coronavirus-masks-tests-ppe.html', 'snippet': 'Blue Flame Medical boasted that it could acquire masks, testing kits and other equipment to respond to the pandemic. State and local governments paid up — and are still waiting for delivery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A company created just six weeks ago by a pair of Republican operatives received hundreds of millions of dollars in payments from desperate state and local governments for coronavirus supplies, but is now facing a federal criminal investigation and a rising chorus of complaints from customers who say their orders never arrived.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/06/us/politics/06dc-virus-contracts1/merlin_171784701_ad46e831-77ab-4f8d-a939-7f255eb507b3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/06/us/politics/06dc-virus-contracts1/merlin_171784701_ad46e831-77ab-4f8d-a939-7f255eb507b3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/06/us/politics/06dc-virus-contracts1/merlin_171784701_ad46e831-77ab-4f8d-a939-7f255eb507b3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/06/us/politics/