': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Climate', 'section_name': 'Climate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hiroko Tabuchi and Beth Gardiner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Beth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gardiner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3480ac28-5896-518b-8e17-44030c2e9e3e', 'word_count': 1120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3480ac28-5896-518b-8e17-44030c2e9e3e'}, {'abstract': 'A preliminary report posted online claimed that a mutation had made the virus more transmissible. Geneticists say the evidence isn’t there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/06/health/coronavirus-mutation-transmission.html', 'snippet': 'A preliminary report posted online claimed that a mutation had made the virus more transmissible. Geneticists say the evidence isn’t there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All viruses mutate, and the coronavirus is no exception. But there is no compelling evidence yet that it is evolving in a way that has made it more contagious or more deadly.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/06/science/06VIRUS-MUTATIONS/merlin_170970642_9446066b-547f-4d31-a3cd-baf5b2ad9371-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 518, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/06/science/06VIRUS-MUTATIONS/merlin_170970642_9446066b-547f-4d31-a3cd-baf5b2ad9371-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 518}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/06/science/06VIRUS-MUTATIONS/merlin_170970642_9446066b-547f-4d31-a3cd-baf5b2ad9371-jumbo.jpg', 'hei