use of the coronavirus. Here’s an alternative that’s easy, clean and good for the climate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/06/climate/new-york-coronavirus-composting.html', 'snippet': 'New York City has suspended its composting program because of the coronavirus. Here’s an alternative that’s easy, clean and good for the climate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New Yorkers have been through a lot over the last couple of months, but this felt personal: The city stopped picking up curbside compost this week and asked residents to instead discard their food scraps and yard waste with their trash.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/06/climate/06CLI-COMPOST/06CLI-COMPOST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/06/climate/06CLI-COMPOST/06CLI-COMPOST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/06/climate/06CLI-COMPOST/06CLI-COMPOST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/06/climate/06CLI-COMPOST/06CLI-COMPOST-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/06/climate/06CLI-COMPOST/06CLI-COMPOST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/06/climate/06CLI-COMPOST/06CLI-COMPOST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/06/climate/06CLI-COMPOST/06CLI-COMPOST-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Compost by My Couch: How (and Why) I Started an Odorless Bin at Home', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Compost', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-06T18:26:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Climate', 'section_name': 'Climate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hiroko Tabuchi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39405772-5f64-5cfa-b8da-0a561e29adb6', 'word_count': 890, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39405772-5f64-5cfa-b8da-0a561e29adb6'}, {'abstract': 'As exhibitions around the world close, or cancel the next stops on their tours, logistical and emotional carnage follow.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/06/arts/design/van-eyck-ghent-cancellation-virus.html', 'snippet': 'As exhibitions around the world close, or cancel the next stops on their tours, logistical and emotional carnage follow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Ghent Altarpiece was never supposed to leave St. Bavo’s Cathedral again. Not after the 15th-century masterpiece was nearly destroyed by rioting Calvinists in 1566. Not after its panels had been stolen at least six times: once by Napoleon, later by the Nazis (who took the whole thing). Church leaders in Ghent, its Belgian home, were overjoyed in 1945, when the altar by Jan van Eyck and his brother Hubert was returned.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/06/arts/06virus-blockbuster1/merlin_167738178_aa8bdefa-9f83-4d2b-8b48-4f2ec3286124-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/06/arts/06virus-blockbuster1/merlin_167738178_aa8bdefa-9f83-4d2b-8b48-4f2ec3286124-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/06/arts/06virus-blockbuster1/merlin_167738178_aa8bdefa-9f83-4d2b-8b48-4f2ec3286124-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/06/arts/06virus-blockbuster1/merlin_167738178_aa8bdefa-9f83-4d2b-8b48-4f2ec3286124-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/06/arts/06virus-blockbuster1/merlin_167738178_aa8bdefa-9f83-4d2b-8b48-4f2ec3286124-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/06/arts/06virus-blockbuster1/merlin_167738178_aa8bdefa-9f83-4d2b-8b48-4f2ec3286124-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/06/arts/06virus-blockbuster1/merlin_167738178_aa8bdefa-9f83-4d2b-8b48-4f2ec3286124-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType