e swerve when we witness the truth, when we become aware. We shift gears and find our way.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/07/magazine/a-poem-about-changing-course.html', 'snippet': 'We swerve when we witness the truth, when we become aware. We shift gears and find our way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If we were picking favorite words, “swerve” would be one of mine, but not the kind where a car slips and goes astray. Swerve as an awakening: to lean over into new knowing — change course in thinking — alter a path, suddenly — be jolted, advised. Ellery Akers’s powerful poems in “Swerve” are prescriptions for awareness, bolts of care. Whether about the last inauguration, war, water, bad teachers or climate change — each poem, as in “At Any Moment … ,” glistens with detail, and attention. Selected by Naomi Shihab Nye.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/magazine/10-mag-poem-1/10-mag-poem-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 596, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/10/magazine/10-mag-poem-1/10-mag-poem-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 596}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/magazine/10-mag-poem-1/10-mag-poem-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 668, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/magazine/10-mag-poem-1/10-mag-poem-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 668, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/magazine/10-mag-poem-1/10-mag-poem-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/10/magazine/10-mag-poem-1/10-mag-poem-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/magazine/10-mag-poem-1/10-mag-poem-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Poem About Changing Course', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wilderness Areas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-07T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellery Akers and Naomi Shihab Nye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellery', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Akers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Naomi', 'middlename': 'Shihab', 'lastname': 'Nye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e54a56cf-5d03-530c-a8e0-acabf936777e', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e54a56cf-5d03-530c-a8e0-acabf936777e'}, {'abstract': 'Two books remind us of other times when humankind suffered from mass contagions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/07/books/review/pandemics-of-the-past-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'Two books remind us of other times when humankind suffered from mass contagions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was, it seemed, the end of the world — and that was before the plague came. In the first decade of the 14th century, the climate was changing, and not for the good. “A physical chill settled on the 14th century at its very start, initiating the miseries to come,” Barbara W. Tuchman wrote in her 1978 book “A Distant Mirror: The Calamitous 14th Century.” “The Baltic Sea froze over twice, 1303 and 1306-07; years followed of unseasonable cold, storms and rains, and a rise in the level of the Caspian Sea.” Known as the Little Ice Age, the shift in weather was mysterious in cause but clear in its devastating effects: Colder weather meant a curtailed growing season, which in turn meant less food, which in the last resort meant people starved to death.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/24/books/Meacham2-01/merlin_145228953_d727b81f-be1b-4c04-b7d8-67648a4aea33-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 428, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/24/books/Meacham2-01/merlin_145228953_d727b81f-be1b-4c04-b7d8-67648a4aea33-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 428}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/24/books/Meacham2-01/merlin_145228953_d727b81f-be1b-4c04-b7d8-67648a4aea33-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/24/books/Meacham2-01/merlin_145228953_d727b81f-be1b-4c04-b7d8-67648a4aea33-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1461, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/24/books/Meacham2-01/Meacham2-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/24/books/Meacham2-01/Meacham2-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/24/books/Meacham2-01/Meacham2-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pandemics of the Past', 'kicker': 'The Long View', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pandemics Past', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plague', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smallpox', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coss, Stephen F (1957- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tuchman, Barbara W', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'A Distant Mirror: The Calamitous 14th Century (Book)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Fever of 1721: The Epidemic That Revolutionized Medicine and American Politics (Book)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-07T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Meacham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meacham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03a14098-c34c-5a18-aa98-887ed5fbd1a0', 'word_count': 1187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03a14098-c34c-5a18-aa98-887ed5fbd1a0'}, {'abstract': 'Parents can help children use the stress of coronavirus shutdowns as an opportunity for growth, experts say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/07/well/family/coronavirus-children-stress-parents.html', 'snippet': 'Parents can help children use the stress of coronavirus shutdowns as an opportunity for growth, experts say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Children may be processing the disruptions in their lives right now in ways the adults around them do not expect: acting out, regressing, retreating or even seeming surprisingly content. Parents need to know that all of this is normal, experts say, and there are some things we can do to help.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/24/well/00kidstress/00kidstress-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/24/well/00kidstress/00kidstress-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/24/well/00kidstress/00kidstress-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/24/well/00kidstress/00kidstress-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/24/well/00kidstress/00kidstress-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/24/well/00kidstress/00kidstress-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/24/well/00kidstress/00kidstress-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Keep Children’s Stress From Turning Into Trauma', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Here to Help; How to Keep Children’s Stress From Turning Into Trauma', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-07T09:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Family', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stacey Steinberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stacey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08dbe998-eb77-57e8-b614-e6ab5ac66db3', 'word_count': 1169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08dbe998-eb77-57e8-b614-e6ab5ac66db3'}, {'abstract': 'Video chats are in. Small talk is out. You don’t have to fret about who picks up the check. And maybe the biggest plus: You’re forced to take things slow.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/07/well/mind/dating-coronavirus-love-relationships.html', 'snippet': 'Video chats are in. Small talk is out. You don’t have to fret about who picks up the check. And maybe the biggest plus: You’re forced to take things slow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’re single and dating, you’re no doubt facing special challenges during this horrid pandemic. But as a biological anthropologist who has spent some 40 years studying romantic love around the world and the brain circuitry of this ancient and universal human passion, I’ve come to recognize that in some ways, coronavirus has given you a gift.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/30/well/well-dating/well-dating-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/04/30/well/well-dating/well-dating-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/30/well/well-dating/well-dating-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/30/well/well-dating/well-dating-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/30/well/well-dating/well-dating-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/04/30/well/well-dating/well-dating-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/30/well/well-dating/well-dating-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Coronavirus Is Changing the Dating Game for the Better', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Single 