llege.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court weighs whether Electoral College electors can vote their preference for president rather than the choice of their state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amid all the well-justified worry during this troubled election season about vote suppression, the most direct threat to having every vote count has been hiding in plain sight: “faithless electors” who might cast their Electoral College votes according to their own preferences rather than for the choice of their states’ voters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/07/opinion/07greenhouse1/merlin_162656070_d28882b2-1d52-4584-80c4-0fb5a8d9ac44-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/07/opinion/07greenhouse1/merlin_162656070_d28882b2-1d52-4584-80c4-0fb5a8d9ac44-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/07/opinion/07greenhouse1/merlin_162656070_d28882b2-1d52-4584-80c4-0fb5a8d9ac44-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/07/opinion/07greenhouse1/merlin_162656070_d28882b2-1d52-4584-80c4-0fb5a8d9ac44-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1345, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/07/opinion/07greenhouse1/07greenhouse1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/07/opinion/07greenhouse1/07greenhouse1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight':