ish their kids during the pandemic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/07/parenting/food-insecurity-children.html', 'snippet': 'How parents in food-insecure households are stretching meals and struggling to nourish their kids during the pandemic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Life was not easy for Tianna Gaines-Turner before the coronavirus pandemic began. When she was out of work for six months last year after having her fourth child, the family, who lives in Northeast Philadelphia and has struggled with periodic homelessness and hunger, relied on her husband’s job as a machine operator at a pill-packing plant, as well as their monthly stipend from the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program, or SNAP, formerly known as food stamps. She eventually returned to her job as a housing stabilization specialist for a Philadelphia nonprofit, but her hours were only part-time and her paycheck came just once a month.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/07/multimedia/07parenting-foodinsecurity/07parenting-foodinsecurity-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/07/multimedia/07parenting-foodinsecurity/07parenting-foodinsecurity-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/07/multimedia/07parenting-foodinsecurity/07parenting-foodinsecurity-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/07/multimedia/07parenting-foodinsecurity/07parenting-foodinsecurity-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1167, 'width': 1750, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':