en after she retired.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/07/nyregion/elizabeth-scholtz-dead.html', 'snippet': 'The first female director of a major botanic garden in the U.S., she was a daily presence at the Brooklyn Botanic Garden even after she retired.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1972, when Elizabeth Scholtz became director of the Brooklyn Botanic Garden, the splendid 52-acre urban garden founded in 1910, she was not only the first female director of a major botanic garden in the United States; she was also one of the few women in charge of a large New York City cultural institution. This made for some awkward collisions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/08/obituaries/07Scholtz1/07Scholtz1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 867, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/08/obituaries/07Scholtz1/07Scholtz1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 867}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/08/obituaries/07Scholtz1/07Scholtz1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/08/obituaries/07Scholtz1/07Scholtz1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1411, 'width': 976, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/08/obituaries/07Scholtz1/07Scholtz1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/08/obituaries/07Scholtz1/07Scholtz1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'ran