ed one of the country’s most intensive door-knocking operations into one of the country’s most intensive screen-pinging operations.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: A Knock at the Door: Invaluable for Turnout, Improbable in 2020', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-05-08T03:04:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/016c63fa-065f-5cab-b1b2-dbda92f939c4', 'word_count': 53, 'uri': 'nyt://article/016c63fa-065f-5cab-b1b2-dbda92f939c4'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections that appeared in print on Friday, May 8, 2020.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/07/pageoneplus/corrections-may-8-2020.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections that appeared in print on Friday, May 8, 2020.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An article on Thursday about the risks of gathering in cooling centers during the pandemic misstated the number of people sleeping without shelter in Phoenix. A survey in January counted almost 4,000 in all of Maricopa County, which includes Phoenix, not in the city of Phoenix alone.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: May 8, 2020', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-05-08T03:21:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e41a21b-6713-545e-92d7-451b1dfad335', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e41a21b-6713-545e-92d7-451b1dfad335'}, {'abstract': 'As the economy melts down, embattled conservatives are testing a political response: saying Democratic climate policies would bring similar pain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/07/climate/coronavirus-republicans-climate-change.html', 'snippet': 'As the economy melts down, embattled conservatives are testing a political response: saying Democratic climate policies would bring similar pain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The coronavirus and the struggle to contain it has tanked the economy, shuttered thousands of businesses and thrown more than 30 million people out of work. As President Trump struggles for a political response, Republicans and their allies have seized on an answer: attacking climate change policies.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/07/climate/00CLI-REPUBLICANS2/merlin_171825000_daaac918-f699-411f-87f6-287e962fe8df-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/07/climate/00CLI-REPUBLICANS2/merlin_171825000_daaac918-f699-411f-87f6-287e962fe8df-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/07/climate/00CLI-REPUBLICANS2/merlin_171825000_daaac918-f699-411f-87f6-287e962fe8df-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/07/climate/00CLI-REPUBLICANS2/merlin_171825000_daaac918-f699-411f-87f6-287e962fe8df-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/07/climate/00CLI-REPUBLICANS2/00CLI-REPUBLICANS2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/07/climate/00CLI-REPUBLICANS2/00CLI-REPUBLICANS2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/07/climate/00CLI-REPUBLICANS2/00CLI-REPUBLICANS2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P. Coronavirus Message: Economic Crisis Is a Green New Deal Preview', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'G.O.P. Aims to Use Pain  Of Shutdown to Tarnish Climate Change Policies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Green New Deal', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-08T03:44:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Climate', 'section_name': 'Climate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e7574af-5a66-5562-899e-dd780734e14f', 'word_count': 1319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e7574af-5a66-5562-899e-dd780734e14f'}, {'abstract': 'A mother who uses sign language sees an expressive upside to the hush that has fallen over the land.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/08/style/modern-love-coronavirus-deaf-motherhood-in-a-quiet-world.html', 'snippet': 'A mother who uses sign language sees an expressive upside to the hush that has fallen over the land.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It took a pandemic for me to finally see my language everywhere. During any disaster, you’ll usually see a sign-language interpreter next to the government officials. But with this disaster being both nationwide and seemingly endless, so is the presence of sign-language interpreters. I watch as their hands create images that flow directly into my brain, as natural as breathing.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/fashion/10VIRUS-MODERN-DEAF/10VIRUS-MODERN-DEAF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 752, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/10/fashion/10VIRUS-MODERN-DEAF/10VIRUS-MODERN-DEAF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 752}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/fashion/10VIRUS-MODERN-DEAF/10VIRUS-MODERN-DEAF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 818, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/fashion/10VIRUS-MODERN-DEAF/10VIRUS-MODERN-DEAF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1635, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/fashion/10VIRUS-MODERN-DEAF/10VIRUS-MODERN-DEAF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/10/fashion/10VIRUS-MODERN-DEAF/10VIRUS-MODERN-DEAF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/fashion/10VIRUS-MODERN-DEAF/10VIRUS-MODERN-DEAF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mothering While Deaf in a Newly Quiet World', 'kicker': 'Modern Love', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mothering in a Newly Quiet World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deafness', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sign Language', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-08T04:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shoshannah Stern', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shoshannah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stern', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd05eace-7df4-534b-b484-0f848360df12', 'word_count': 1572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd05eace-7df4-534b-b484-0f848360df12'}, {'abstract': 'A suburban fashionista falls for a Hollywood punk in this remake of the cult 1983 rom-com.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/08/movies/valley-girl-review.html', 'snippet': 'A suburban fashionista falls for a Hollywood punk in this remake of the cult 1983 rom-com.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The material world of “Valley Girl,” a fizzy and fun remake of the 1983 cult rom-com, sprawls across contrasting ’80s neighborhoods. Julie (Jessica Rothe) and her posse live in the San Fernando Valley, where they shop and shriek in a luridly glowing mall. But over the hill, the grimier world of Hollywood is home to her soon-to-be boyfriend Randy (Josh Whitehouse), whose pierced and tatted pals prefer moshing at punk shows.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/08/arts/valleygirl1/merlin_172117548_58944b4e-cb5d-404a-95c6-cd81a7570559-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/08/arts/valleygirl1/merlin_172117548_58944b4e-cb5d-404a-95c6-cd81a7570559-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/08/arts/valleygirl1/merlin_172117548_58944b4e-cb5d-404a-95c6-cd81a7570559-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/08/arts/valleygirl1/merlin_172117548_58944b4e-cb5d-404a-95c6-cd81a7570559-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/08/arts/valleygirl1/valleygirl1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/08/arts/valleygirl1/valleygirl1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credi