 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telemedicine', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-08T14:21:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margot Sanger-Katz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margot', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sanger-Katz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3742284e-6ca7-5162-b9bc-9c4394367f0a', 'word_count': 1242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3742284e-6ca7-5162-b9bc-9c4394367f0a'}, {'abstract': 'The featured comedians, including Jerry Seinfeld, developed much of their material before the quarantine. Their bits can lighten your mood in unexpected ways.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/08/arts/television/coronavirus-best-new-comedy-specials.html', 'snippet': 'The featured comedians, including Jerry Seinfeld, developed much of their material before the quarantine. Their bits can lighten your mood in unexpected ways.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Laughter is the best medicine” is a cliché that has been skewered so many times it’s easy to forget the animating truth behind it. No, a joke will not save us, but it can provide solace, and not just by lightening the mood. In a time when many are isolated and suffering, it’s easy to get stuck in destructive mental patterns. The utility of jokes is that they are perfectly engineered to trick minds out of ruts, manipulate thoughts in one direction or another, a Rube Goldberg device delighting through distraction. The day will come when all the new comedy will have been made in a world after the pandemic, but we are not there yet. Most of the new specials, developed before the crisis, seem like they arrived from another world. For those tired of this one, it can be nice to visit. Here are a few recent examples.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/09/arts/08COMEDY-ROUNDUP-LEAD/merlin_172084317_255d919f-1e32-497d-bb75-d792ff8a5c24-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/09/arts/08COMEDY-ROUNDUP-LEAD/merlin_172084317_255d919f-1e32-497d-bb75-d792ff8a5c24-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/09/arts/08COMEDY-ROUNDUP-LEAD/merlin_172084317_255d919f-1e32-497d-bb75-d792ff8a5c24-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/09/arts/08COMEDY-ROUNDUP-LEAD/merlin_172084317_255d919f-1e32-497d-bb75-d792ff8a5c24-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/09/arts/08COMEDY-ROUNDUP-LEAD/08COMEDY-ROUNDUP-LEAD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/09/arts/08COMEDY-ROUNDUP-LEAD/08COMEDY-ROUNDUP-LEAD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/09/arts/08COMEDY-ROUNDUP-LEAD/08COMEDY-ROUNDUP-LEAD-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '5 New Comedy Specials to Remind You of the Old Normal', 'kicker': 'On Comedy', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Remember The Old Normal?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Escola, Cole', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kindler, Andy (1956- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seinfeld, Jerry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': '23 Hours to Kill (TV Program)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'AKA (Radio Program)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Who the Hell is Dwayne Kennedy? (Radio Program)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Hence the Humor (Radio Program)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaplan, Myq', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Dwayne (Comedian)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Help! I'm Stuck! (Web-Original Program)", 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-08T14:29:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Zinoman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinoman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/261ef789-4635-5619-bf17-a51bf3d36f7b', 'word_count': 1228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/261ef789-4635-5619-bf17-a51bf3d36f7b'}, {'abstract': 'Cook for mom, and make pancakes, a springy asparagus soup, or a carrot cake, or cook for yourself, and make a flawless bacon, egg and cheese sandwich.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/08/dining/what-to-cook-this-weekend.html', 'snippet': 'Cook for mom, and make pancakes, a springy asparagus soup, or a carrot cake, or cook for yourself, and make a flawless bacon, egg and cheese sandwich.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. A long time ago, when I used to ride an electric motorbike through crowded traffic so I could get to a subway station where I shared a rickety elevator with a lot of people before getting on a train car with even more, so that I could travel into the heart of Times Square to go to work, making my way down 40th Street against a heaving tide of people coming from the Port Authority, I sometimes stopped at the deli across the street from the newspaper and ordered a bacon, egg and cheese sandwich.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/28/dining/28COOKING-ALMOND-BERRY-LAYER-CAKE1/28COOKING-ALMOND-BERRY-LAYER-CAKE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/05/28/dining/28COOKING-ALMOND-BERRY-LAYER-CAKE1/28COOKING-ALMOND-BERRY-LAYER-CAKE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/28/dining/28COOKING-ALMOND-BERRY-LAYER-CAKE1/28COOKING-ALMOND-BERRY-LAYER-CAKE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/28/dining/28COOKING-ALMOND-BERRY-LAYER-CAKE1/28COOKING-ALMOND-BERRY-LAYER-CAKE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/28/dining/28COOKING-ALMOND-BERRY-LAYER-CAKE1/28COOKING-ALMOND-BERRY-LAYER-CAKE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/05/28/dining/28COOKING-ALMOND-BERRY-LAYER-CAKE1/28COOKING-ALMOND-BERRY-LAYER-CAKE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/05/28/dining/28COOKING-ALMOND-BERRY-LAYER-CAKE1/28COOKING-ALMOND-BERRY-LAYER-CAKE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Cook This Weekend', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-08T14:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/812973a4-cfc5-5eab-a22c-8461fbb407fa', 'word_count': 659, 'uri': 'nyt://article/812973a4-cfc5-5eab-a22c-8461fbb407fa'}, {'abstract': 'In “Yes No Maybe So,” by Becky Albertalli and Aisha Saeed, two teenagers from different backgrounds feel a spark while canvassing for a local politician.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/08/books/review/yes-no-maybe-so-becky-albertalli-aisha-saeed.html', 'snippet': 'In “Yes No Maybe So,” by Becky Albertalli and Aisha Saeed, two teenagers from different backgrounds feel a spark while canvassing for a local politician.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For every generation categorized as “lazy” or “uninformed,” along comes a group of young people to Shut. That. Down.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/17/books/review/17-BKS-COLBERT_KIDS/17-BKS-COLBERT_KIDS-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 441, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/17/books/review/17-BKS-COLBERT_KIDS/17-BKS-COLBERT_KIDS-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 441, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/17/books/review/17-BKS-COLBERT_KIDS/17-BKS-COLBERT_KIDS-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/17/books/review/17-BKS-COLBERT_KIDS/17-BKS-COLBERT_KIDS-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/17/books/review/17-BKS-COLBERT_KIDS/17-BKS-COLBERT_KIDS-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Working for Social Change, High School Students Find a Social Life', 'kicker': 'Children’s Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Yes No Maybe So (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Albertalli, Becky', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saeed, Aisha', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-08T14:33:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brandy Colbert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brandy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Colbert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3b108e1-5cc4-572d-adbc-cad9f6ff12fd', 'word_count': 646, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3b108e1-5cc4-572d-adbc-cad9f6ff12fd'}, {'abstract': 'In Abby Sher’s “Miss You Love You Hate You Bye,” two best friends prove to be their own worst enemies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/08/books/review/miss-you-love-you-hate-you-bye-abby-sher.html', 'snippet': 'In Abby Sher’s “Miss You Love You Hate You Bye,” two best friends prove to be their own worst enemies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All hail the best friend! That person we confide in and listen to without fear or judgment. The one with whom we share in-jokes. The one who holds our hand, metaphorically and sometimes literally, through the murky patches. As the cliché goes, we don’t always know where this person ends and we begin. During a time of insecurity, surging hormones and confusion about who we are (I’m talking about adolescence, though it can go on forever), the best friend may be the most stabilizing force in our lives. Pinky swear.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/17/books/review/17-BKS-DOLL_KIDS/17-BKS-DOLL_KIDS-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 896, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'i