'', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/98a190d4-5389-5773-9018-0632756b3df4', 'word_count': 375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98a190d4-5389-5773-9018-0632756b3df4'}, {'abstract': 'Records kept by medical examiners in Florida offer a window into how the coronavirus has killed more than 1,600 people there. Many died at home.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/08/us/coronavirus-florida-medical-examiner-records.html', 'snippet': 'Records kept by medical examiners in Florida offer a window into how the coronavirus has killed more than 1,600 people there. Many died at home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — A 71-year-old woman with nausea who was sent home from the emergency room, even though a doctor wanted to admit her. A 63-year-old nurse who was self-isolating while she waited for results from her coronavirus test. A 77-year-old man who was prescribed antibiotics by a doctor in another state for his fever and dry cough.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/08/us/00VIRUS-FLORIDA/00VIRUS-FLORIDA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/08/us/00VIRUS-FLORIDA/00VIRUS-FLORIDA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/08/us/00VIRUS-FLORIDA/00VIRUS-FLORIDA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/08/us/00VIRUS-FLORIDA/00VIRUS-FLORIDA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/08/us/00VIRUS-FLORIDA/00VIRUS-FLORIDA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/08/us/00VIRUS-FLORIDA/00VIRUS-FLORIDA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/08/us/00VIRUS-FLORIDA/00VIRUS-FLORIDA-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Found Unresponsive at Home’: Grim Records Recount Lonely Deaths', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Found Unresponsive at Home’: Grim Records Recount Lonely Deaths', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeSantis, Ron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-08T17:32:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Mazzei, Rebecca Halleck and Richard A. Oppel Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mazzei', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Halleck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Oppel', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e983c08-c740-5a6b-a328-81e5942d977b', 'word_count': 1317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e983c08-c740-5a6b-a328-81e5942d977b'}, {'abstract': 'In February, the hotelier Philomena Schurer Merckoll toasted her new creative showcase, Design Marrakech, with a gathering at her guesthouse, Riad Mena.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/08/t-magazine/design-marrakech-philomena-schurer-merckoll.html', 'snippet': 'In February, the hotelier Philomena Schurer Merckoll toasted her new creative showcase, Design Marrakech, with a gathering at her guesthouse, Riad Mena.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a few faint rain drops began to fall in the courtyard of Riad Mena, a seven-room guesthouse in the Marrakesh medina, the hotelier Philomena Schurer Merckoll looked skyward, assessing the likelihood of a downpour. This was in February, when a seasonal shower was the biggest threat to a social gathering, and at risk beneath the citrus trees were white linen sofas and red silk-embroidered floor cushions, laid out for cocktail hour before a dinner in honor of Marrakesh’s design talent. But with artworks arriving and her guests expected, she shrugged at the massing clouds, determined the evening should go on. The furniture was taken inside and then reassembled an hour later once the shower had passed. Looking back now, from a radically altered world of shelter-in-place orders and social distancing, guests fondly recall the evening as one of the last when they were able to mingle freely with friends old and new. “It’s wonderful to remember that dinner now,” said Schurer Merckoll late last month. “It feels so special because it gives me hope for more positive times to come.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/27/t-magazine/24tmag-riadmena-slide-JB1H/24tmag-riadmena-slide-JB1H-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/04/27/t-magazine/24tmag-riadm