 there ever was one, though at least the man is well versed in the behaviors of lapdogs.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/opinion/10Senior/merlin_169973271_fb9a408a-5845-4c51-8ac4-2e643ca7a05a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/10/opinion/10Senior/merlin_169973271_fb9a408a-5845-4c51-8ac4-2e643ca7a05a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/opinion/10Senior/merlin_169973271_fb9a408a-5845-4c51-8ac4-2e643ca7a05a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/opinion/10Senior/merlin_169973271_fb9a408a-5845-4c51-8ac4-2e643ca7a05a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/opinion/10Senior/10Senior-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/10/opinion/10Senior/10Senior-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/10/opinion/10Senior/10Senior-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Does Anyone Actually Work for Trump?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Trump Administration Is Made of Swiss Cheese', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Security Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-10T22:45:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Senior', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Senior', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/2862bfca-fea4-504c-b87a-451824ac4c4e', 'word_count': 911, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2862bfca-fea4-504c-b87a-451824ac4c4e'}, {'abstract': 'The president wants a new cold war to deflect attention from his failures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/10/opinion/china-coronavirus-trump.html', 'snippet': 'The president wants a new cold war to deflect attention from his failures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before the pandemic, before the Great Recession, before proliferating hurricanes and fires, the United States began a global war on terrorism. Its leaders fixated on a shadowy enemy abroad as life at home crumbled for millions of Americans. The war on terrorism did not end terrorism; the war itself became endless. What it did shatter was the myth that a triumphant United States could bend the world to its will.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype