in her in pondering what makes the genre so great — and so vital during a pandemic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/11/arts/television/workplace-comedies.html', 'snippet': 'A writer asks the minds behind “Veep,” “Brooklyn Nine-Nine” and other office comedies to join her in pondering what makes the genre so great — and so vital during a pandemic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To begin, a confession: My husband, an essential worker, goes to an office every weekday. He walks about a mile, navigating the sidewalks like a player in some virus-inflected Frogger game, and rides a lonely elevator to an empty 10th floor suite. A staggered schedule guarantees that he works alone — which means no pleasantries, no gossip, no box of doughnuts in the kitchenette just because. And even the thought of this office — bereft, doughnut-less — makes me extremely jealous.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/12/arts/11office-sitcoms1/merlin_172286328_bdd11128-a19f-47e2-98e5-3b1605e7210a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/12/arts/11office-sitcoms1/merlin_172286328_bdd11128-a19f-47e2-98e5-3b1605e7210a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/12/arts/11office-sitcoms1/merlin_172286328_bdd11128-a19f-47e2-98e5-3b1605e7210a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 637, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/12/arts/11office-sitcoms1/merlin_172286328_bdd11128-a19f-47e2-98e5-3b1605e7210a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1275, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'lega