e, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/09/multimedia/09xp-cash-pix/09xp-cash-pix-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/09/multimedia/09xp-cash-pix/09xp-cash-pix-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/09/multimedia/09xp-cash-pix/09xp-cash-pix-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/09/multimedia/09xp-cash-pix/09xp-cash-pix-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 769, 'width': 1159, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/09/multimedia/09xp-cash-pix/09xp-cash-pix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/09/multimedia/09xp-cash-pix/09xp-cash-pix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/09/multimedia/09xp-cash-pix/09xp-cash-pix-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lesson of the Day: ‘Teenager, an Aspiring Detective, Returns $135,000 He Found’', 'kicker': 'current events', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-05-11T12:01:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shannon Doyne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shannon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doyne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed77041e-59cd-554a-85e4-b653ef58504b', 'word_count': 649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed77041e-59cd-554a-85e4-b653ef58504b'}, {'abstract': 'When children help with the education of a brother or sister with special needs, the outcomes are often good for both.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/11/parenting/children-sibling-disability.html', 'snippet': 'When children help with the education of a brother or sister with special needs, the outcomes are often good for both.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not long after my mother learned that my brother, David, was autistic, she began what she called “little school”: sessions in which she taught him to draw faces, cut with scissors, read and cook. He was 4, I was 2. I recently asked her how she balanced David’s needs with mine. “You were the teacher’s assistant,” she said. “I was trying to make you feel important.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/11/multimedia/parenting-siblings/parenting-siblings-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/11/multimedia/parenting-siblings/parenting-siblings-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/11/multimedia/parenting-siblings/parenting-siblings-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/11/multimedia/parenting-siblings/parenting-siblings-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1166, 'width': 1750, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/11/multimedia/parenting-siblings/parenting-siblings-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/11/multimedia/parenting-siblings/parenting-siblings-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/11/multimedia/parenting-siblings/parenting-siblings-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Growing Up Alongside a Sibling With a Disability', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Intellectual Disabilities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Special Education', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-11T12:27:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Parenting', 'section_name': 'Parenting', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keren Landman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c589aded-6002-5ca5-8d10-f097800abfd8', 'word_count': 1170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c589aded-6002-5ca5-8d10-f097800abfd8'}, {'abstract': 'When will anyone else be able to watch our children?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/11/parenting/coronavrius-childcare.html', 'snippet': 'When will anyone else be able to watch our children?', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few weeks ago, my 3-year-old discovered that she could initiate FaceTime calls on her own. She can’t read, but she can identify the avatars of her grandparents, aunts and uncles, and her dad’s goofiest friends from a purloined iPad. At first this was mildly alarming — how long before my 3-year-old FaceTimes one of our bosses, or some rando we met once in 2007 whose number is still in our contact list? But with minor supervision we realized that we could pawn her and her big sister off on physically distant relatives for 30 minute spurts, and get a much-needed break for ourselves.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/04/multimedia/04parenting-integratingchildcare/04parenting-integratingchildcare-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/04/multimedia/04parenting-integratingchildcare/04parenting-integratingchildcare-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/04/multimedia/04parenting-integratingchildcare/04parenting-integratingchildcare-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/04/multimedia/04parenting-integratingchildcare/04parenting-integratingchildcare-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0,