 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/11/realestate/2-8-million-homes-in-california.html', 'snippet': 'A 1938 storybook home in Mill Valley, a new house in San Jose and a midcentury hacienda in Pasadena.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mill Valley, a Marin County city 14 miles north of San Francisco, has long been popular with Bay Area residents seeking access to nature. In the early 20th century, the Mount Tamalpais and Muir Woods Railway transported tourists from downtown Mill Valley to the eastern peak of Mount Tamalpais, and by the mid-20th century the city had become a magnet for Bay Area artists and musicians. This house is a 10-minute drive from the Muir Woods National Monument and about half an hour from Stinson Beach.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/11/realestate/11WYG-CA-slide-RBHN/11WYG-CA-slide-RBHN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 353, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/11/realestate/11WYG-CA-slide-RBHN/11WYG-CA-slide-RBHN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 353}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/11/realestate/11WYG-CA-slide-RBHN/11WYG-CA-slide-RBHN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 602, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/11/realestate/11WYG-CA-slide-RBHN/11WYG-CA-slide-RBHN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1205, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/11/realestate/11WYG-CA-slide-RBHN/11WYG-CA-slide-RBHN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legac