elina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Delkic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Carole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3297b73-78db-5710-ac9b-8908fa52f383', 'word_count': 1437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3297b73-78db-5710-ac9b-8908fa52f383'}, {'abstract': 'A new cookbook profiles the makers at this popular outdoor food festival, on hold until the pandemic passes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/11/dining/queens-night-market-cookbook.html', 'snippet': 'A new cookbook profiles the makers at this popular outdoor food festival, on hold until the pandemic passes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Queens Night Market is the subject of a new cookbook, “The World Eats Here.” Each of the 88 recipes, and the accompanying profiles, is crammed with compelling details. They tell stories of breakfast in Colombia through arepas with scrambled eggs; Guyanese pine tarts made with fresh, not canned fruit; kopytka potato gnocchi from Kika Radz, who missed her mother’s Polish specialties; Myo Thway’s circuitous route to making ohno kaukswe, Burmese noodle soup, at the market; and Wanda Chiu’s Hong Kong soy sauce noodles. The homestyle recipes are not simplified but are easy to follow, assuming you can find the ingredients (there are tips); the book is divided in sections for the Americas, Europe, Africa and the Middle East, and Asia.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/13/dining/11burner-book/merlin_172204929_91981402-311b-4b26-9fea-81ac712e4c8f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/13/dining/11burner-book/merlin_172204929_91981402-311b-4b26-9fea-81ac712e4c8f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 629}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/13/dining/11burner-book/merlin_172204929_91981402-311b-4b26-9fea-81ac712e4c8f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 978, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/13/dining/11burner-book/merlin_172204929_91981402-311b-4b26-9fea-81ac712e4c8f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1955, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/13/dining/11burner-book/11burner-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/13/dining/11burner-book/11burner-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/13/dining/11burner-book/11burner-book-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Relive Memories of the Queens Night Market', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Savor: The Queens Night Market Springs to Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Queens Night Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "The World Eats Here: Amazing Food and the Inspiring People Who Make It at New York's Queens Night Market (Book)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garner, Storm', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wang, John (Entrepreneur)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-11T20:08:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa96fc71-4e1d-586c-85e5-bf365c6636ea', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa96fc71-4e1d-586c-85e5-bf365c6636ea'}, {'abstract': 'The cases are the latest in a series the court has had before it considering the relationship between church and state.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/11/us/supreme-court-religious-schools.html', 'snippet': 'The cases are the latest in a series the court has had before it considering the relationship between church and state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Supreme Court heard arguments on Monday on how broadly federal employment discrimination laws apply to schools run by churches in two cases that will give the court another opportunity to rule on the proper relationship between church and state, a topic that has deeply engaged the justices.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/11/us/politics/11dc-scotus-religion/merlin_172259466_8249aa28-4524-4aea-9526-850866f5b132-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/11/us/politics/11dc-scotus-religion/merlin_172259466_8249aa28-4524-4aea-9526-850866f5b132-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/202