ne, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68f7f9ec-9183-586c-bfd7-f74957fcc576', 'word_count': 1389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68f7f9ec-9183-586c-bfd7-f74957fcc576'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on whether schools should adopt a policy of universal “credit/no credit” this semester — and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/12/magazine/despite-the-pandemic-my-college-is-allowing-grades-isnt-that-unfair.html', 'snippet': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on whether schools should adopt a policy of universal “credit/no credit” this semester — and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am student at a New England liberal arts college that was considering a universal credit/no-credit grading policy in light of the inequalities wrought by the pandemic. Everyone has left campus, so all of the equalizing properties of a residential college are now gone, and students are experiencing lots of extra stress and trauma. Faculty ultimately voted down this universal standard in favor of an opt-in credit/no-credit option, a decision students suspect was influenced by the fact that colleges that have decided on universal pass/fail policies have been subject to lawsuits initiated by students who want either grades or refunds. It’s worth noting that the universal credit/no-credit proposal received overwhelming support from students versus the opt-in policy.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/17/magazine/17Ethicist/17Ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 336, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/17/magazine/17Ethicist/17Ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 336}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/17/magazine/17Ethicist/17Ethicist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 574, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/17/magazine/17Ethicist/17Ethicist-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1148, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/17/magazine/17Ethicist/17Ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/17/magazine/17Ethicist/17Ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/17/magazine/17Ethicist/17Ethicist-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite the Pandemic, My College Is Allowing Grades. Isn’t That Unfair?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Despite the Pandemic, My College Is Allowing Grades This Semester. Isn’t That Unfair?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grading of Students', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-12T09:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kwame Anthony Appiah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kwame', 'middlename': 'Anthony', 'lastname': 'Appiah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4f62105-5a97-52b8-8b77-166ba6bced01', 'word_count': 1396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4f62105-5a97-52b8-8b77-166ba6bced01'}, {'abstract': 'As the coronavirus forces many of us to conduct more of our lives online, nest cams reassure us that there can be value in parasocial companionship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/12/magazine/how-watching-bald-eagles-build-a-nest-prepared-me-for-the-pandemic.html', 'snippet': 'As the coronavirus forces many of us to conduct more of our lives online, nest cams reassure us that there can be value in parasocial companionship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last May a hummingbird landed in a tree right outside my kitchen window, wiped her beak against a branch and flew off. Moments later she returned to dab at the same spot. My wife and I happened to be standing nearby, and for several minutes we watched the scene repeat itself. The hummingbird was building herself a nest, one lichen chip and strand of spider silk at a time. By day’s end the nest was complete; in a few weeks we saw two little beaks pointing up from the nest’s fuzzy lip. The babies got bigger, then learned to fly and then the nest was empty. It clung there for months until rainfall finally dislodged it.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/17/magazine/17mag-LOR-image1/17mag-LOR-image1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 437, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/17/magazine/17mag-LOR-image1/17mag-LOR-image1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 437}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/17/magazine/17mag-LOR-image1/17mag-LOR-image1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/17/magazine/17mag-LOR-image1/17mag-LOR-image1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1491, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/17/magazine/17mag-LOR-image1/17mag-LOR-image1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/17/magazine/17mag-LOR-image1/17mag-LOR-image1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/17/magazine/17mag-LOR-image1/17mag-LOR-image1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Watching Bald Eagles Build a Nest Prepared Me for the Pandemic', 'kicker': 'Letter of Recommendation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nest Cams', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spiders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eggs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hummingbirds', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-12T09:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonah Weiner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23204c3b-85af-5508-9652-bce00fb02369', 'word_count': 975, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23204c3b-85af-5508-9652-bce00fb02369'}, {'abstract': 'With grown children back under their parents’ roof in the pandemic, there are issues of independence, privacy and housekeeping to navigate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/12/well/family/young-adults-parents-quarantine-virus.html', 'snippet': 'With grown children back under their parents’ roof in the pandemic, there are issues of independence, privacy and housekeeping to navigate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeremy Kauffman, 21, was enjoying his junior year at Kenyon College when he had to move back home two months ago. It’s the longest he’s lived under his parents’ roof in two years, but it’s not the 4,000-square-foot house he grew up in. His parents, thinking they were about to be empty nesters, had just downsized to a nearby place half the size, in Cleveland Heights, Ohio. They’ve been there with their three kids finishing up the school year online from “any free spaces available,” said his mother, Lucene Wisniewski.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/05/well/00adult-kids1/00adult-kids1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/05/well/00adult-kids1/00adult-kids1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/05/well/00adult-kids1/00adult-kids1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/05/well/00adult-kids1/00adult-kids1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1151, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/05/well/00adult-kids1/00adult-kids1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/05/well/00adult-kids1/00adult-kids1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/05/well/00adult-kids1/00adult-kids1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Young Adults, Quarantining With Parents Turns Back Time', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Relationships', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-12T09:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Family', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Halpert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Halpert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc75534c-398a-5d9e-bb65-b889ac638828', 'word_count': 1095, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc75534c-398a-5d9e-bb65-b889ac638828'}, {'abstract': 'Wistful words from the actor Alec Baldwin, the comedian Amber Ruffin, the Rev. Al Sharpton, the chef Amanda Cohen, the assemblywoman Yuh-Line Niou and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/12/nyregion/coronavirus-closed-new-yorkers-miss.html', 'snippet': 'Wistful words from the actor Alec Baldwin, the comedian Amber Ruffin, the Rev. Al Sharpton, the chef Amanda Cohen, the assemblywoman Yuh-Line Niou and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seven weeks have passed since New York City, fleeing the coronavirus, put up a collective closed-for-business sign and locked itself away inside the strange, timeless bubble of the shutdown. The crisis, by any standard, has been costly: More than 19,000 New Yorkers have already lost their lives, and tens, if not hundreds, of thousands more have lost their livelihoods.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Hardcore New Yorkers Really Miss', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Here’s What New Yorkers Really Miss', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-12T09:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Feuer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feuer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97e571d1-1909-5037-9289-c8aee83f5739', 'word_count': 1675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97e571d1-1909-5037-9289-c8aee83f5739'}, {'abstract': 'The lifestyle blogger spoke about isolation, leisure and internet trolls from her country home in Norfolk, England.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/12/style/paula-sutton-hill-house-vintage.html', 'snippet': 'The lifestyle blogger spoke about isolation, leisure and internet trolls from her country home in Norfolk, England.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paula Sutton is the latest luminary of cottagecore, a corner of the internet immersed in transcendent scenes of rural life. On Instagram, where she posts as @hillhousevintage, the 50-year-old influencer chronicles the pleasures of entertaining, decorating and gardening from her home in rural Norfolk, England.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/17/fashion/12PAULA-HILLHOUSE-1/12PAULA-HILLHOUSE-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/17/fashion/12PAULA-HILLHOUSE-1/12PAULA-HILLHOUSE-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/17/fashion/12PAULA-HILLHOUSE-1/12PAULA-HILLHOUSE-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/17/fashion/12PAULA-HILLHOUSE-1/12PAULA-HILLHOUSE-1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/17/fashion/12P