school.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every Times reader experiences the newspaper in a different way — some start with the front-page headlines, others with the Travel section and still others with the Magazine. At The Learning Network, we have been creating different ways for students to engage with The Times, too — for example, by responding to a writing prompt, watching a short film or interpreting a graph. With this choice board, we wanted to visually showcase many of the easy-to-use activities we offer teenagers every week during the school year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/12/learning/ChoiceBoardLN/ChoiceBoardLN-articleLarge.png', 'height': 775, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/12/learning/ChoiceBoardLN/ChoiceBoardLN-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 775}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/12/learning/ChoiceBoardLN/ChoiceBoardLN-jumbo.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 793, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/12/learning/ChoiceBoardLN/ChoiceBoardLN-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1799, 'width': 1392, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/12/learning/ChoiceBoardLN/ChoiceBoardLN-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/12/learning/ChoiceBoardLN/ChoiceBoardLN-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/12