: 'Discrimination', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vigilantes', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-12T23:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Yancy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yancy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e15ea12-61b2-5da2-a37e-c64f177723a2', 'word_count': 1428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e15ea12-61b2-5da2-a37e-c64f177723a2'}, {'abstract': 'The virtual art fair tries to condense 160 galleries onto your phone screen. Can art hold your attention amid the infinite scroll?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/12/arts/design/frieze-new-york-online.html', 'snippet': 'The virtual art fair tries to condense 160 galleries onto your phone screen. Can art hold your attention amid the infinite scroll?', 'lead_paragraph': 'An experienced art dealer can recite the cities in order, like the Stations of the Cross: January in Taipei, February in Mexico City, March in Hong Kong or Maastricht, May in New York and on down the art market Via Dolorosa to Miami Beach in December. These cities’ art fairs — Art Basel, Frieze, TEFAF and the rest — have become the stopovers of the global art cavalcade, bringing contemporary painting and sculpture to new audiences, clogging the local airports with private jets, and dragging along an auxiliary band of couch-surfing curators and critics.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/14/arts/12frieze-review10/merlin_172427994_4c9864d0-0b45-4f78-bc8f-4f57e8c01467-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 329, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/14/arts/12frieze-review10/merlin_172427994_4c9864d0-0b45-4f78-bc8f-4f57e8c01467-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 329}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/14/arts/12frieze-review10/merlin_172427994_4c9864d0-0b45-4f78-bc8f-4f57e8c01467-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 561, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/14/arts/12frieze-review10/merlin_172427994_4c9864d0-0b45-4f78-bc8f-4f57e8c01467-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1122, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/14/arts/12frieze-review10/12frieze-review10-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/14/arts/12frieze-review10/12frieze-review10-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/14/arts/12frieze-review10/12frieze-review10-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My Weekend Binge Online at Frieze', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taking a Scroll Through an Online Art Fair', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frieze New York', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gallery Association Los Angeles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bader, Darren', '