'byline': {'original': 'By Todd Haugh and Suneal Bedi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Todd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haugh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Suneal', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bedi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac5238e5-3c10-5e3a-b0b0-229c4a408d12', 'word_count': 568, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac5238e5-3c10-5e3a-b0b0-229c4a408d12'}, {'abstract': 'A letter from inside Marion Correctional Institution is the voice of those locked in cages and discarded during this pandemic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/13/opinion/coronavirus-prison-outbreak.html', 'snippet': 'A letter from inside Marion Correctional Institution is the voice of those locked in cages and discarded during this pandemic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have been wondering what to say about the horror of Covid-19 behind bars. Much has already been written about the scale of the crisis, the moral argument for freeing people from prisons and jails, and the utter inadequacy of the response in many states, including New York.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/13/opinion/13Alexander/13Alexander-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/13/opinion/13Alexander/13Alexander-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/13/opinion/13Alexander/13Alexander-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05