: 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a051c83-58fa-51cb-aa41-79376dc2ac1d', 'word_count': 708, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a051c83-58fa-51cb-aa41-79376dc2ac1d'}, {'abstract': 'The federal government doesn’t seem willing to mobilize, so states will have to do the heavy lifting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/13/opinion/indiana-reopening-coronavirus-testing.html', 'snippet': 'The federal government doesn’t seem willing to mobilize, so states will have to do the heavy lifting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INDIANAPOLIS — One of the most frustrating things about this pandemic is that we still don’t know how many people have been truly infected. We know how many people have tested positive, but that’s not the same thing, because limits in testing don’t give us a full picture. It would require a full statewide, random sample study to allow us to see what’s going on.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/13/opinion/13carroll1/merlin_172294797_fb394f56-ae41-4eba-a48c-0398f4718ceb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/13/opinion/13carroll1/merlin_172294797_fb394f56-ae41-4eba-a48c-0398f4718ceb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/13/opinion/13carroll1/merlin_172294797_fb394f56-ae41-4eba-a48c-0398f4718ceb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/13/opinion/13carroll1/merlin_172294797_fb394f56-ae41-4eba-a48c-0398f4718ceb-superJumbo.jpg', 'hei