 of his era can also be theoretical. Take his “A Man Escaped.” The American “Escape From Alcatraz” is a good companion piece.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Writing about the hard-edged American filmmaker Don Siegel (“Dirty Harry”), the critic Andrew Sarris once made an offhand observation about Siegel’s 1979 “Escape From Alcatraz,” starring Clint Eastwood. Siegel, he wrote, seemed “to have been inspired by Robert Bresson’s ‘A Man Escaped’ (1956).”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/14/arts/14gateway-bresson2/merlin_172452957_ea10c2c0-60a0-4119-877b-108b31d8ac7f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 339, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/14/arts/14gateway-bresson2/merlin_172452957_ea10c2c0-60a0-4119-877b-108b31d8ac7f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 339}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/14/arts/14gateway-bresson2/merlin_172452957_ea10c2c0-60a0-4119-877b-108b31d8ac7f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 578, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/14/arts/14gateway-bresson2/merlin_172452957_ea10c2c0-60a0-4119-877b-108b31d8ac7f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 621, 'width': 1100, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/14/arts/14gateway-bresson2/merlin_172452957_ea10c2c0-60a0-4119-877b-108b31d8ac7f-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/14/arts/14gateway-bresson2/merlin_172452957_ea10c2c0-60a0-4119-877b-108b31d8ac7f-