er in London is streaming a recent hit. And on Amazon, Kristen Stewart plays the actress Jean Seberg in “Seberg.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'BARBER SHOP CHRONICLES Stream on Nationaltheatre.org.uk. Barbershops are portrayed as communal spaces where patrons hang out and talk about politics, relationships and masculinity — and maybe also get their hair cut — in Inua Ellams’s “Barber Shop Chronicles,” a play that was a hit in London in 2017. The story bridges six barbershops in six cities, focusing on conversations in each shop over the course of a day. The fleet-footed script is based on recordings of conversations Ellams made in barbershops in Africa and London. “The men were just laughing whilst talking about really crazy issues,” Ellams said in an interview with The New York Times last year. “I had one rule: If a topic comes up three times in three different countries, then it has to go into the play.” This production, recorded during the show’s run at the National Theater in London, is streaming until late next week as part of a series of free programming being offered during the pandemic.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/15/arts/15tvcol-barbershopchronicles/merlin_123225413_32ada86a-6c9d-428c-8d3e-08cbee775ec5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/15/arts/15tvcol-barbershopchronicles/merlin_123225413_32ada86a-6c9d-428c-8d3e-08cbee775ec5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/15/arts/15tvcol-barbershopchronicles/merlin_123225413_32ada86a-6c9d-428c-8d3e-08cbee775ec5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'su