value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-15T09:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca Carroll', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carroll', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3ff469d-a75f-59cd-b813-36e6b81e6baf', 'word_count': 1226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3ff469d-a75f-59cd-b813-36e6b81e6baf'}, {'abstract': 'From Agatha Christie to Raymond Chandler to Patricia Highsmith, classic detective stories are given new life in audio form.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/15/books/review/classic-detective-audiobooks-agatha-christie-raymond-chandler-partricia-highsmith.html', 'snippet': 'From Agatha Christie to Raymond Chandler to Patricia Highsmith, classic detective stories are given new life in audio form.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am, as we all are, stuck at home these days. Back in mid-March I assumed I would spend much of my time in lockdown reading — still and always my favorite activity, ideal for an indefinite period of mandatory solitude imposed by, say, a pandemic. This has not been the case. I’ve read fewer books over the past few weeks than I have over any comparable stretch that I can remember. Focus has evaporated. The cognitive load of living through the coronavirus has gone straight for my literary jugular.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New Yo