3, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71f858e6-568f-5f6c-a297-a711ba5d3b65'}, {'abstract': 'And we know how that worked out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/15/opinion/coronavirus-trump-hoover.html', 'snippet': 'And we know how that worked out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Additional economic assistance is the only thing that can keep the U.S. economy from falling into a second Great Depression, and with interest rates near zero, the government has all the fiscal capacity it needs to borrow the trillions necessary to relieve the pain. But Congress, or rather congressional Republicans, won’t budge. After backing the $2 trillion CARES Act in March, they believe they’ve done enough for now.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/15/opinion/15bouie1/merlin_172505388_ff66d7b7-5e5c-4691-bf32-b10cc20de29c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 493, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/15/opinion/15bouie1/merlin_172505388_ff66d7b7-5e5c-4691-bf32-b10cc20de29c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 493}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/15/opinion/15bouie1/merlin_172505388_ff66d7b7-5e5c-4691-bf32-b10cc20de29c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 841, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/15/opinion/15bouie1/merlin_172505388_ff66d7b7-5e5c-4691-bf32-b10cc20de29c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1682, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/15/opinion/15bouie1/15bouie1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStand