ge, people doing what they do, but right now it is. I am trying to be patient with myself as life uncoils itself back out into the world. I hope you are, too, and that whatever you’re doing, you take some time to read some amazing journalism.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/16/multimedia/16weekend-reads-promo/16weekend-reads-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/16/multimedia/16weekend-reads-promo/16weekend-reads-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/16/multimedia/16weekend-reads-promo/16weekend-reads-promo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/16/multimedia/16weekend-reads-promo/16weekend-reads-promo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1334, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/16/multimedia/16weekend-reads-promo/16weekend-reads-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/16/multimedia/16weekend-reads-promo/16weekend-reads-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/16/multimedia/16weekend-reads-promo/16weekend-reads-promo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '11 of Our Best Weekend Reads', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Little Richard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stiller, Jerry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-15T12:37:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SpecialSections', 'section_name': 'Briefing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kaly Soto', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kaly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Soto', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ccad726-6fd0-503d-9764-f7a84d23a0b9', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ccad726-6fd0-503d-9764-f7a84d23a0b9'}, {'abstract': 'The showrunners for the NBC thriller discuss how and why they hired animators to finish the season after the pandemic brought production to a halt. The finale airs Friday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/15/arts/television/the-blacklist-animated-season-finale.html', 'snippet': 'The showrunners for the NBC thriller discuss how and why they hired animators to finish the season after the pandemic brought production to a halt. The finale airs Friday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In mid-March, when the coronavirus pandemic shut New York City down, television production came to a sudden halt, sabotaging whole seasons for some shows and postponing season finales for others. But NBC’s “The Blacklist,” which follows James Spader’s Raymond “Red” Reddington as he helps the F.B.I. bring down the world’s most nefarious criminals, soldiered on.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'i