22b83384-a9fb-5aa3-a2be-744007bcfcd3', 'word_count': 638, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22b83384-a9fb-5aa3-a2be-744007bcfcd3'}, {'abstract': 'The agency granted emergency clearance for a testing kit that allows a consumer to take a nasal sample at home and send it to a laboratory for the diagnosis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/16/health/fda-clears-another-coronavirus-testing-kit-for-use-at-home.html', 'snippet': 'The agency granted emergency clearance for a testing kit that allows a consumer to take a nasal sample at home and send it to a laboratory for the diagnosis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Food and Drug Administration on Saturday granted emergency clearance for a coronavirus testing kit that will enable individuals to take a nasal sample at home and send it to a laboratory for diagnostic testing, the second such approval it has made.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.D.A. Clears Another Coronavirus Testing Kit for Use at Home', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Medical)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Laboratories and Scientific Equipment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Everlywell Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shuren, Jeffrey E', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-16T21:20:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheila Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edbff224-0f24-5a98-a26c-551c02c76dd9', 'word_count': 524, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edbff224-0f24-5a98-a26c-551c02c76dd9'}, {'abstract': 'Byron Walden slows our roll with a tough Sunday puzzle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/16/crosswords/daily-puzzle-2020-05-17.html', 'snippet': 'Byron Walden slows our roll with a tough Sunday puzzle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUNDAY PUZZLE — We are fast approaching Byron Walden’s 100th puzzle for The Times, and he’s prolific elsewhere (including the American Crossword Puzzle Tournament). I think today’s construction is an escalation in the unthemed Sunday crossword monster construction race, as it has only 122 entries, tied with a beast from last year by Frank Longo (fewer answers make puzzles tougher to solve and absolute bears to build, as a rule). As its title intimates, this grid also has 177 “open squares,” which are empty squares that don’t touch any black block, even diagonally, third only to a 218 Patrick Berry Sunday puzzle and the aforementioned Longo puzzle. Joel Fagliano has made a 124-answer Sunday puzzle in the last year as well; all of these have been unthemed. Perhaps one day we’ll get a collaboration between all of these constructors with 42 spans and no black squares at all, and someone will still drop a “too easy!” in the comments.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/17/crosswords/17wordplay-usain/17wordplay-usain-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 347, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/17/crosswords/17wordplay-usain/17wordplay-usain-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 347}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/17/crosswords/17wordplay-usain/17wordplay-usain-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 593, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 