ml', 'snippet': 'Corrections that appeared in print on Sunday, May 17, 2020.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An article on Page 13 about the TNT series “Snowpiercer” misstates the class status of Andre Layton, the character played by Daveed Diggs. Layton is a member of the bottom class, known as tailies, not the third class, which is higher.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: May 17, 2020', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-05-17T02:45:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc3524fa-7e35-5506-91e1-e9c12728003d', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc3524fa-7e35-5506-91e1-e9c12728003d'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Sunday, May 17, 2020.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/16/todayspaper/quotation-of-the-day-i-cant-turn-my-brain-off.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Sunday, May 17, 2020.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The virus scares the hell out of our guys. And now, when they go home to decompress, instead they and their spouses are home-schooling. The spouse has lost a job, and is at wit’s end. The kids are screaming. Let me tell you: The tension level in the crews is through the roof.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: ‘I Can’t Turn My Brain Off’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-05-17T02:48:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_o