 Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6d4c340-5bb9-511d-b96a-42d24de794c6', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6d4c340-5bb9-511d-b96a-42d24de794c6'}, {'abstract': 'Hook’s Cheese in Mineral Point, Wis., is among the few Cheddar makers aging its cheeses past two years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/18/dining/hooks-cheese-20-year-cheddar.html', 'snippet': 'Hook’s Cheese in Mineral Point, Wis., is among the few Cheddar makers aging its cheeses past two years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Buying Cheddar? Even with handmade clothbound farmstead products, finding anything aged more than two years is a challenge. That’s why Hook’s Aged Cheddar Cheese  from Mineral Point, Wis., is so special; some are aged up to 20 years. The bright orange cheese has an aroma of toffee and herbs, is moderately sharp and delivers an alluring hint of crunch, a hallmark of some well-aged cheeses. These attributes define the company’s 15-year-old cheese and are intensified in the rare, limited 20-year-old.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/20/dining/18burner-cheese/18burner-cheese-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 419, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/20/dining/18burner-cheese/18burner-cheese-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 419}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/20/dining/18burner-cheese/18burner-cheese-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 715, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None