ticle/314e289d-f4a9-5121-be00-944ec4648da3'}, {'abstract': 'But a Police Department investigation found that a sergeant had violated department rules in other ways when he detained Dr. Armen Henderson outside his home last month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/18/us/armen-henderson-miami-police.html', 'snippet': 'But a Police Department investigation found that a sergeant had violated department rules in other ways when he detained Dr. Armen Henderson outside his home last month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — A Miami police officer was justified in handcuffing and detaining a black doctor outside his home last month, an internal investigation has found, though the review also determined that the officer had violated department rules by yelling at the doctor and not wearing a face mask.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/18/multimedia/18xp-doctor/18xp-doctor-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/18/multimedia/18xp-doctor/18xp-doctor-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/18/multimedia/18xp-doctor/18xp-doctor-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/18/multimedia/18xp-doctor/18xp-doctor-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/18/multimedia/18xp-doctor/18xp-doctor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/18/multimedia/18xp-doctor/18xp-doctor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/18/multimedia/18xp-doctor/18xp-doctor-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuffing of Black Miami Doctor Was Justified, Review Finds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Officer Who Handcuffed Black Doctor Is Cleared', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Miami (Fla)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Racial Profiling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Henderson, Armen (1985- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-18T18:56:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Express', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Johnny Diaz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Johnny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Diaz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ab18c95-b246-57c6-af67-780c88d146e1', 'word_count': 724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ab18c95-b246-57c6-af67-780c88d146e1'}, {'abstract': 'The Tesla chief executive is putting the safety of employees on the line.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/18/opinion/elon-musk-tesla-factory.html', 'snippet': 'The Tesla chief executive is putting the safety of employees on the line.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Elon Musk, the chief executive of the carmaker Tesla, is something different to everyone. For having mass-produced cool all-electric vehicles, he has been a hero to coastal environmentalist liberals. Small-government conservatives have lionized him for thumbing his nose at regulators. He has been likened to the superhero Iron Man, and sci-fi aficionados love the billionaire for his dreams of colonizing Mars.Online, his exhortations can cause markets to shudder or soar and prompt lawsuits and investigations. His cryptic tweet over the weekend to “Take the red pill” aroused speculation he was signaling a rightward turn — Ivanka Trump seemed to agree — or that he is simply a fan of “The Matrix.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/18/opinion/18Bensinger/18Bensinger-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/18/opinion/18Bensinger/18Bensinger-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/18/opinion/18Bensinger/18Bensinger-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 711, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/18/opinion/18Bensinger/18Bensinger-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1422, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/18/opinion/18Bensinger/18Bensinger-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/18/opinion/18Bensinger/18Bensinger-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/18/opinion/18Bensinger/18Bensinger-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Elon Musk’s Latest Gambit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus Reopenings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tesla Motors Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Musk, Elon', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALAMEDA COUNTY (CALIF)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fremont (Calif)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-18T19:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bensinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bensinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a72a4221-26d8-57ad-9b94-a5ea4bb0103c', 'word_count': 1093, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a72a4221-26d8-57ad-9b94-a5ea4bb0103c'}, {'abstract': 'The mothers who live at St. Ann’s are essential.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/18/opinion/coronavirus-homeless.html', 'snippet': 'The mothers who live at St. Ann’s are essential.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a small auditorium at St. Ann’s Center for Children, Youth and Families in Hyattsville, Md., 26-year-old Susana Chiang and I talk softly through our masks. Nearby is a well-loved plastic playhouse, where Ms. Chiang’s 4-year-old daughter is preparing us pretend food. She serves invisible ice cream and pasta with pepper and eggs. Children always seem taken with the essential vocations — food service, mail delivery, health care, parenthood — as though they’re born with a sense of what’s important in the world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/07/opinion/00bruenig1/merlin_172106133_84ac321e-5459-474c-8505-3439c2fe86af-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/07/opinion/00bruenig1/merlin_172106133_84ac321e-5459-474c-8505-3439c2fe86af-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/07/opinion/00bruenig1/merlin_172106133_84ac321e-5459-474c-8505-3439c2fe86af-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/07/opinion/00bruenig1/merlin_172106133_84ac321e-5459-474c-8505-3439c2fe86af-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/07/opinion/00bruenig1/00bruenig1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/07/opinion/00bruenig1/00bruenig1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/07/opinion/00bruenig1/00bruenig1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Only Home Her Daughter Has Ever Known', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domestic Violence', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "St. Ann's Center for Children, Youth and Families", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-18T19:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Bruenig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruenig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/30d14171-a335-5118-9f96-f4175d7b3d5a', 'word_count': 1035, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30d14171-a335-5118-9f96-f4175d7b3d5a'}, {'abstract': 'Pandemic or not, immigrants’ work has always been essential.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/18/opinion/coronavirus-essential-workers-immigrants.html', 'snippet': 'Pandemic or not, immigrants’ work has always been essential.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOXBOROUGH, Mass. — Recently, as I drove home from a long day of work as a home health aide, a police cruiser appeared behind me with lights flashing. It was 10 p.m. and the roads were nearly empty. As I pulled to the side of the road, my heart was pounding.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'sub