e forced to use scarce foreign currency to make unsustainable debt payments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/19/opinion/argentina-debt-negotiation-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'Governments won’t be able to contain the pandemic if they are forced to use scarce foreign currency to make unsustainable debt payments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Argentina is currently engaged in intense negotiations with its creditors over at least $65 billion in government debt. The most important part of that negotiation, which can make or break Argentina’s economic recovery, is foreign currency debt. That is mostly in dollars, and mostly owned by foreigners.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/19/opinion/19Weisbrot/merlin_172284534_81063ad2-bdc5-4d0a-a0be-a95da045233f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/19/opinion/19Weisbrot/merlin_172284534_81063ad2-bdc5-4d0a-a0be-a95da045233f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/19/opinion/19Weisbrot/merlin_172284534_81063ad2-bdc5-4d0a-a0be-a95da045233f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/19/opinion/19Weisbrot/merlin_172284534_81063ad2-bdc5-4d0a-a0be-a95da045233f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/19/opinion/19Weisbrot/19Weisbrot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumb