.G.B.T.Q. community are missing out on an important moment of visibility and acceptance. We want to hear from them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the first protests and parades in New York City 50 years ago to the celebrations that span the world today, Pride has always been about being seen — not just by the L.G.B.T.Q. community but by everyone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/18/us/pride-cancelled-callout/pride-cancelled-callout-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/18/us/pride-cancelled-callout/pride-cancelled-callout-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/18/us/pride-cancelled-callout/pride-cancelled-callout-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/18/us/pride-cancelled-callout/pride-cancelled-callout-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/18/us/pride-cancelled-callout/pride-cancelled-callout-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/18/us/pride-cancelled-callout/pride-cancelled-callout-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/18/us/pride-cancelled-callout/pride-cancelled-callout-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Does It Mean to You That Pride Is Called Off?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parades', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-20T19:31:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pierre-Antoine Louis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pierre-antoine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Louis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a3f2e85-c42f-54f2-9716-8e6ae2d707b7', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a3f2e85-c42f-54f2-9716-8e6ae2d707b7'}, {'abstract': 'Then ask questions of its playwright, Dominique Morisseau, and The New York Times critic who reviewed the first production.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/20/theater/pipeline-play-stream.html', 'snippet': 'Then ask questions of its playwright, Dominique Morisseau, and The New York Times critic who reviewed the first production.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dominique Morisseau’s gripping 2017 drama “Pipeline” — which is available to stream for free through Friday — is as of-the-moment as this morning’s headlines. The concerns of its heroine, Nya, about her teenage son, Omari, have everything to do with his being a black youth in the United States in the 21st century.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/20/arts/20pipeline-1/merlin_123744362_c43cdf9e-0a16-45a0-83b9-9fd729b4