ml', 'snippet': 'Even when businesses like mine can open up for real, it will be very hard to keep them going in a socially distanced world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On March 13, as New York City schools let out for what turned out to be their last official day and offices were telling their employees to work from home, I came down with an ominous fever and chills, and my business partner and I closed our two Brooklyn bar-restaurants. By the next week I would be diagnosed with Covid-19, and the week after that I would develop pneumonia. I spent four weeks bedridden, isolated from my family, at times immobilized with terror that I wouldn’t survive the night. When the virus released its grip and I could finally sit up in bed, my first impulse was to email my staff: We’re back in business!', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/22/opinion/22cecchini/merlin_158593797_fc2a3b85-a64b-4324-ab70-84b5b6779809-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/22/opinion/22cecchini/merlin_158593797_fc2a3b85-a64b-4324-ab70-84b5b6779809-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/22/opinion/22cecchini/merlin_158593797_fc2a3b85-a64b-4324-ab70-84b5b6779809-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/22/opinion/22cecchini/merlin_158593797_fc2a3b85-a64b-4324-ab70-84b5b6779809-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'i