d6007', 'word_count': 1051, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa0554ad-9186-5aaf-a750-d5a451bd6007'}, {'abstract': 'Sure, you could make your own. But if you’re in the mood to buy, most of these also include a charitable element.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/22/at-home/best-face-masks-fashion-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'Sure, you could make your own. But if you’re in the mood to buy, most of these also include a charitable element.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Retail as a whole has declined rapidly over the last two months, but one segment of the struggling industry has defied the trend: face masks. In early April, the Centers for Disease Control began encouraging Americans to wear face masks outside their homes. By then, a crop of do-it-yourself solutions had already emerged, intended to abate shortages of medical-grade personal protective equipment among those on the front lines of the fight against the coronavirus. More than a month later, it’s apparent that social distancing — and thus, mask-wearing — will continue to be necessary throughout the summer. (Of course, in some parts of the world, face masks are already worn daily.)', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/24/multimedia/24ah-masks2/24ah-masks2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 347, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/24/multimedia/24ah-masks2/24ah-masks2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 347}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/24/multimedia/24ah-masks2/24ah-masks2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 591, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/24/multimedia/24ah-masks2/24a