6b-5059-8be4-aef8743f80b7', 'word_count': 1684, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b139ef58-eb6b-5059-8be4-aef8743f80b7'}, {'abstract': 'The cure-all debate over the cannabis compound has distracted from the serious — and seriously odd — back story of how cannabidiol conquered the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/23/sunday-review/coronavirus-cbd-oil.html', 'snippet': 'The cure-all debate over the cannabis compound has distracted from the serious — and seriously odd — back story of how cannabidiol conquered the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Long before CBD had become a trendy wellness elixir found in juice and moisturizer and ice cream and dog treats; before corporate chains like Walgreens and Sephora had decided to sell it; and way before Kim Kardashian West had thrown a CBD-themed baby shower, a ragtag crew of activists, doctors, writers and marijuana farmers met up on an early winter evening in 2011. They sat in a circle at a house in the hills a few hours north of San Francisco — where wine country becomes weed country — to discuss the therapeutic potential of CBD, and how to get people to take it seriously.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/24/opinion/24lewisRingo/merlin_172715970_3da6a474-ff5a-42c2-864e-e4759cf9747b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/24/opinion/24lewisRingo/merlin_172715970_3da6a474-ff5a-42c2-864e-e4759cf9747b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/24/opinion/24lewisRingo/merlin_172715970_3da6a474-ff5a-42c2-864e-e4759cf9747b-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'super