one, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus Reopenings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mosques', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bank', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Places of Worship', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-24T14:17:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher F. Schuetze, Constant Méheut and Adam Rasgon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Schuetze', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Constant', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Méheut', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rasgon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/486f98cc-4c8e-5180-8cbe-a352c43a5c63', 'word_count': 1156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/486f98cc-4c8e-5180-8cbe-a352c43a5c63'}, {'abstract': 'Make Momofuku’s bo ssam, or take the Memorial Day holiday to bake an Earl Grey tea cake, peanut butter brownies, or an easy rhubarb trifle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/24/dining/what-to-cook-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'Make Momofuku’s bo ssam, or take the Memorial Day holiday to bake an Earl Grey tea cake, peanut butter brownies, or an easy rhubarb trifle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. It’s funny, the things that bring happiness in these weird, unsettled times. I thrill to routine: the morning bike ride to see the sun rise; the hurried lunch alongside my children in the kitchen; Kai Ryssdal on the radio in the evenings, as I chop and steam, slice and fry. Weekends unmoor me. Anything could happen. Nothing might. So I shower a pork butt with salt and sugar and let it cure on Saturday, and Sunday it spends in the oven: my weekly bo ssam (above), David Chang and Peter Meehan’s gift to the world. At least I’ve got that.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/magazine/15eat1_span/15eat1_span-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 445, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/15/magazine/15eat1_span/15eat1_span-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 445}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/magazine/15eat1_span/15eat1_span-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 753, 'width': 1015, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/magazine/15eat1_span/15eat1_span-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 753, 'width': 1015, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/magazine/15eat1_span/15eat1_span-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/15/magazine/15eat1_span/15eat1_span-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thum