'Quotation of the Day for Monday, May 25, 2020.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I guess other people expect us to set our futures on fire to keep their fear warm. I think that’s incredibly selfish — if you’re that fearful, then just stay home.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: Virus at Its Deadliest in the Strongholds of Democrats', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-05-25T10:11:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/edcc588f-f456-5c89-a667-462c410397b8', 'word_count': 57, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edcc588f-f456-5c89-a667-462c410397b8'}, {'abstract': 'A country known for litigiousness has gingerly restarted court proceedings, and lawyers are bracing for chaos.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/25/world/europe/spain-courts-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'A country known for litigiousness has gingerly restarted court proceedings, and lawyers are bracing for chaos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRID — A flood of new court cases, some with little precedent, is expected to deluge a Spanish judicial system already gasping for breath, bogged down by delays and lagging in technology.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/24/world/24virus-spain-legal01/merlin_172706775_31422f74-eb0a-4fbd-b59b-3d144bd9a4f0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/24/world/24virus-spain-legal01/merlin_172706775_31422f74-eb0a-4fbd-b59b-3d144bd9a4f0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xla