utensils, but resistance is strong. Sharing food with personal chopsticks is one way Chinese people express intimacy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At Chilli Kitchen in Beijing, spicy and mouth-numbing Sichuan dishes are laid out family style. Using red chopsticks, diners dive into steaming bowls of pork wontons bathed in fragrant chili oil and sesame seeds, and rummage through platters filled with dried red chili peppers to unearth juicy bits of roasted fish.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/21/world/00virus-chopsticks-top1/merlin_172699593_feda49c9-3ada-4236-a890-a6c57ccf6fc1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/21/world/00virus-chopsticks-top1/merlin_172699593_feda49c9-3ada-4236-a890-a6c57ccf6fc1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/21/world/00virus-chopsticks-top1/merlin_172699593_feda49c9-3ada-4236-a890-a6c57ccf6fc1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/21/world/00virus-chopsticks-top1/merlin_172699593_feda49c9-3ada-4236-a890-a6c57ccf6fc1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/21/world/00virus-chopsticks-top1/00virus-chopsticks-top1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/21/world/00virus-chopsticks-top1/00virus-chopsticks-top1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/21/world/00virus-chopsticks-top1/00virus-chopsticks-top1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Coronavirus Threatens China’s Devotion to Chopsticks and Sharing Food', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chopstick ‘Revolution’ Faces an Uphill Fight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chopsticks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chinese Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'SARS (Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hygiene and Cleanliness', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-25T14:25:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Qin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Qin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61adc178-d67a-509e-9df4-cda1c8b7572a', 'word_count': 1308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61adc178-d67a-509e-9df4-cda1c8b7572a'}, {'abstract': 'Take time to think about those we’ve lost, then cook for those nearest to you.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/25/dining/the-paradox-of-memorial-day.html', 'snippet': 'Take time to think about those we’ve lost, then cook for those nearest to you.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. One hundred and one years ago, the American ambassador to France, Hugh Wallace, invited President Woodrow Wilson to speak at a Memorial Day ceremony near Paris, to honor American doughboys killed during World War I. The president had been in France for months attending to the peace process and was in ill health, a victim of the flu epidemic that had begun to roil the world the previous year. Still, he rallied:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/03/dining/Salt-and-Pepper-Beef-Ribs/Salt-and-Pepper-Beef-Ribs-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/04/03/dining/Salt-and-Pepper-Beef-Ribs/Salt-and-Pepper-Beef-Ribs-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/03/dining/Salt-and-Pepper-Beef-Ribs/Salt-and-Pepper-Beef-Ribs-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/03/dining/Salt-and-Pepper-Beef-Ribs/Salt-and-Pepper-Beef-Ribs-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/03/dining/Salt-and-Pepper-Beef-Ribs/Salt-and-Pepper-Beef-Ribs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/04/03/dining/Salt-and-Pepper-Beef-Ribs/Salt-and-Pepper-Beef-Ribs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/03/dining/Salt-a