'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bf341be-d16a-5006-86de-2b522e0fd10f', 'word_count': 987, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bf341be-d16a-5006-86de-2b522e0fd10f'}, {'abstract': 'Modern Love in miniature, featuring reader-submitted stories of no more than 100 words.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/26/style/tiny-modern-love-stories-coronavirus-its-ok-if-you-meet-someone.html', 'snippet': 'Modern Love in miniature, featuring reader-submitted stories of no more than 100 words.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A very drunk man won’t stop telling me about trains. The Cape Town summer is hot, the night sticky, my drink warm. This gay bar will surely sink, given the number of heaving bodies shoved inside it. I nod at the train-talker, plotting an escape, and you appear. Your accent is cute, your beard cuter, and you tell the train guy that we’re here together. Suddenly, we are here together. It isn’t a lie; it’s a prophecy, and a good one at that. Ten years, three countries, five cities, four dogs and two toddlers later, we’re still here, together. — Michael McClelland', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/05/fashion/05TINYLOVE-ILLO6/05TINYLOVE-ILLO6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/05/fashion/05TINYLOVE-ILLO6/05TINYLOVE-ILLO6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/05/fashion/05TINYLOVE-ILLO6/05TINYLOVE-ILLO6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/05/fashion/05TINYLOVE-ILLO6/05TINYLOVE-ILLO6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/05/fashion/05TINYLOVE-ILLO6/05TINYLOVE-ILLO6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/05/fashion/05TINYLOVE-ILLO6/05TINYLOVE-ILLO6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/05/fashion/05TINYLOVE-ILLO6/05TINYLOVE-ILLO6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tiny Love Stories: ‘It’s OK if You Meet Someone’', 'kicker': 'Modern Love', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Modern Love (Times Column)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Relationships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Widows and Widowers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-26T19:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cd943d3-bf24-52a2-88e9-58dd92baf9cb', 'word_count': 491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cd943d3-bf24-52a2-88e9-58dd92baf9cb'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Vanishing Half,” her follow-up to “The Mothers,” Brit Bennett writes about twin sisters from Louisiana who set out in very different directions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/26/books/review-vanishing-half-brit-bennett.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Vanishing Half,” her follow-up to “The Mothers,” Brit Bennett writes about twin sisters from Louisiana who set out in very different directions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No nation can lay lasting claim to a genre, save perhaps one. The story of racial passing is a uniquely and intensely American form. From its earliest avatars, the 19th-century novel “Clotel,” for example, to Langston Hughes’s short stories and Nella Larsen’s 1929 masterpiece, “Passing,” to the melodrama films of the 1950s, like “Pinky” and “Imitation of Life,” it is a story central to the American imagination, re-examined and retold so regularly it seems to enjoy a perpetual heyday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/books/26BOOKBENNETT1/26BOOKBENNETT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 833, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/27/books/26BOOKBENNETT1/26BOOKBENNETT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 833}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/books/26BOOKBENNETT1/26BOOKBENNETT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/books/26BOOKBENNETT1/26BOOKBENNETT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1253, 'width': 902, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/books/26BOOKBENNETT1/26BOOKBENNETT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/27/books/26BOOKBENNETT1/26BOOK