rms live music for a tiny audience, chiming 53 bells to help keep up morale during a health crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/27/world/canada/ottawa-peace-tower-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'In a belfry high above Ottawa, the Dominion Carillonneur performs live music for a tiny audience, chiming 53 bells to help keep up morale during a health crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OTTAWA — Finding a spot on the sweeping lawn in front of Canada’s ornately Gothic Parliament buildings to hear a concert this month was not a problem in the middle of a pandemic.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/25/world/00canada-bells-dispatch4/merlin_170357175_d5c92c56-57a2-434d-b02b-3fbd8c58ccf3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/25/world/00canada-bells-dispatch4/merlin_170357175_d5c92c56-57a2-434d-b02b-3fbd8c58ccf3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/25/world/00canada-bells-dispatch4/merlin_170357175_d5c92c56-57a2-434d-b02b-3fbd8c58ccf3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/25/world/00canada-bells-dispatch4/merlin_170357175_d5c92c56-57a2-434d-b02b-3fbd8c58ccf3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/25/world/00canada-bells-dispatch4/00canada-bells-dispatch4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/25/world/00canada-bells-dispatch4/00canada-bells-dispatch4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/25/world/00canada-bells-dispatch4/00canada-bells-dispatch4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada’s ‘Voice of the Nation’ Rings Out in a Capital Quieted by a Virus', 'kicker': 'Ottawa Dispatch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Tower  Rings Out  In a Capital Gone Quiet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Musical Instruments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bells', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ottawa (Ontario)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCrady, Andrea (Musician)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-27T07:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Canada', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1938699c-0124-5f67-8863-11b8cbb2600a', 'word_count': 1133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1938699c-0124-5f67-8863-11b8cbb2600a'}, {'abstract': 'From his home in New York, Vikas Khanna, the TV host, writer and former executive chef at Junoon, is running a relief effort that distributes food to vulnerable Indians.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/27/world/asia/vikas-khanna-india-hungry.html', 'snippet': 'From his home in New York, Vikas Khanna, the TV host, writer and former executive chef at Junoon, is running a relief effort that distributes food to vulnerable Indians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — He has cooked for the Obamas, hosted TV shows with Gordon Ramsay, written 25 culinary books and created sumptuous meals that cost nearly $40,000 each.But in the past two months, Vikas Khanna, a Michelin-starred chef, has turned his focus to India’s hungry, providing millions of meals to poor Indians who have suffered greatly under the coronavirus lockdown.Mr. Khanna was born in India and came to New York as an aspiring chef 20 years ago, first paying his dues as a dishwasher and delivery man. As parts of India slid into a humanitarian crisis in recent months, with millions of out-of-work people desperate for food, Mr. Khanna watched the news from his apartment in Manhattan and grew despondent.“We’ve totally failed our people,” he said in an interview last week. “I wanted to show that solidarity still exists.”“My mom lives alone in Amritsar,” he added, “and I thought: What if she needed help and there was no one to help her?”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/world/27india-chef-chef1/merlin_172871007_934f09ff-438d-4a7d-9b9a-3bdc32685ac2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/27/world/27india-chef-chef1/merlin_172871007_934f09ff-438d-4a7d-9b9a-3bdc32685ac2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/world/27india-chef-chef1/merlin_172871007_934f09ff-438d-4a7d-9b9a-3bdc32685ac2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/world/27india-chef-chef1/merlin_172871007_934f09ff-438d-4a7d-9b9a-3bdc32685ac2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/world/27india-chef-chef1/27india-chef-chef1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/27/world/27india-chef-chef1/27india-chef-chef1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/world/27india-chef-chef1/27india-chef-chef1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Chef Has a Michelin Star and a Mission: Feeding Millions in India’s Lockdown', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'He Has a Michelin Star and a Mission: Send Help to His Native India', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khanna, Vikas (1971- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-27T07:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shalini Venugopal Bhagat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shalini', 'middlename': 'Venugopal', 'lastname': 'Bhagat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/871404dc-0cf0-5002-adc4-6ff53a3ee625', 'word_count': 1032, 'uri': 'nyt://article/871404dc-0cf0-5002-adc4-6ff53a3ee625'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Wednesday, May 27, 2020.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/27/todayspaper/quotation-of-the-day-chess-cheers-as-a-master-recovers-and-plays.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Wednesday, May 27, 2020.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Chess players know what it’s like to be in a bad position, to suffer. I realized it was going to be a long game, with no easy victory.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: Chess Cheers as a Master Recovers, and Plays', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-05-27T07:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d36cc76c-8c17-5d5f-afb7-c7337af075f3', 'word_count': 61, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d36cc76c-8c17-5d5f-afb7-c7337af075f3'}, {'abstract': 'Many sought to oppose a bill that would threaten prison for disrespecting the Chinese national anthem, the latest expression of public anger at Beijing’s encroachment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/27/world/asia/hong-kong-protest-china-anthem.html', 'snippet': 'Many sought to oppose a bill that would threaten prison for disrespecting the Chinese national anthem, the latest expression of public anger at Beijing’s encroachment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — The protesters wanted to surround the city’s government offices, but a smothering police presence forced them to abandon that plan. They tried to block traffic in the financial district at lunchtime, but the police pelted the crowd with rubber bullets. They gathered in malls to chant protest slogans, but were later rounded up and herded on to police buses.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/world/27hongkong-promo/merlin_172871157_e6f89e65-df3c-48c9-a91f-aa8e4fab29a9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/27/world/27hongkong-promo/merlin_172871157_e6f89e65-df3c-48c9-a91f-aa8e4fab29a9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/world/27hongkong-promo/merlin_172871157_e6f89e65-df3c-48c9-a91f-aa8e4fab29a9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/world/27hongkong-promo/merlin_172871157_e6f89e65-df3c-48c9-a91f-aa8e4fab29a9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/world/27hongkong-promo/27hongkong-1sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/27/world/27hongkong-promo/27hongkong-1sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit