'headline': {'main': '‘Overtaken by Aliens’: India Faces Another Plague as Locusts Swarm', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'India, Already Reeling, Faces Voracious Plague of Locusts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grasshoppers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jaipur (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-27T08:52:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Gettleman and Suhasini Raj', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gettleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Suhasini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Raj', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/834ef645-46d0-56e3-b834-7252a00966c2', 'word_count': 649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/834ef645-46d0-56e3-b834-7252a00966c2'}, {'abstract': 'In “Entangled Life,” the biologist Merlin Sheldrake shines a celebratory spotlight on the little understood features and functions of fungal networks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/27/books/review-entangled-life-fungi-merlin-sheldrake.html', 'snippet': 'In “Entangled Life,” the biologist Merlin Sheldrake shines a celebratory spotlight on the little understood features and functions of fungal networks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Finishing the manuscript for a book is usually the consummation of years of work, and when writers emerge on the other side, they often try to do something appropriately celebratory. For his new book, “Entangled Life: How Fungi Make Our Worlds, Change Our Minds, and Shape Our Futures,” the young fungal biologist Merlin Sheldrake decided on a ritual I had never heard of, much less fathomed.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/28/books/27BOOKSHELDRAKE1/27BOOKSHELDRAKE1-articleLarge.png', 'height': 828, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/28/books/27BOOKSHELDRAKE1/27BOOKSHELDRAKE1-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 828}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/28/books/27BOOKSHELDRAKE1/27BOOKSHELDRAKE1-jumbo.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 742, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/28/books/27BOOKSHELDRAKE1/27BOOKSHELDRAKE1-superJumbo.png', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1484, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/28/books/27BOOKSHELDRAKE1/27BOOKSHELDRAKE1-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/28/books/27BOOKSHELDRAKE1/27BOOKSHELDRAKE1-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/28/books/27BOOKSHELDRAKE1/27BOOKSHELDRAKE1-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Whether You’re Making a Meal or Cleaning