 Tucker Carlson’s Fox News Channel show. Over dystopian scenes of people being wheeled on gurneys, filling out unemployment-insurance forms and standing in long lines while wearing surgical masks, lachrymose string music plays. “Under the leadership of Donald Trump, our country is weaker and sicker and poorer,” a narrator intones. We see abandoned warehouses and an upside-down flag flapping listlessly outside a ramshackle home. “And now,” the narrator continues, “Americans are asking: If we have another four years like this, will there even be an America?”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/31/magazine/31Mag-Screenland-01/31Mag-Screenland-01-articleLarge.png', 'height': 208, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/31/magazine/31Mag-Screenland-01/31Mag-Screenland-01-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 208}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/31/magazine/31Mag-Screenland-01/31Mag-Screenland-01-jumbo.png', 'height': 355, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/31/magazine/31Mag-Screenland-01/31Mag-Screenland-01-superJumbo.png', 'height': 711, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/31/magazine/31Mag-Screenland-01/31Mag-Screenland-01-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/31/magazine/31Mag-Screenland-01/31Mag-Screenland-01-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/31/magazine/31Mag-Screenland-01/31Mag-Screenland-01-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Anti-Trump Ad Is Just the Beginning of a Narrative Free-for-All', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Say Anything', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-27T09:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Zengerle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zengerle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4f093aa-535b-5700-86a4-a0ace7f52f1e', 'word_count': 1150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4f093aa-535b-5700-86a4-a0ace7f52f1e'}, {'abstract': 'You can sip it or have it with rice and yogurt. You can treat it like a soup or a glass of savory juice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/27/magazine/soup-so-vibrant-its-called-the-elixir-of-life.html', 'snippet': 'You can sip it or have it with rice and yogurt. You can treat it like a soup or a glass of savory juice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I love rasam, but I don’t really know how to neatly condense its description into a clause between commas. Is it a soup? Yes and no. You might have some hot rasam as one part of a big, elaborate meal, or just with a little bit of rice in front of your laptop, or sip on it plain, lying on the sofa under a blanket, when you’re feeling unwell. You might come home to an empty fridge and throw it together with what’s in the pantry, dissolving a packet of rasam powder from the supermarket into boiling water. Every time I slurp my aunt’s tomato rasam — a warm, tart, soothing infusion — seasoned with fried mustard seeds and curry leaves, plus a little rice and yogurt on the side, I think I should get into the habit of making it, as she does, almost every day.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/31/magazine/31mag-eat-image/31mag-eat-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 452, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/31/magazine/31mag-eat-image/31mag-eat-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 452}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/31/magazine/31mag-eat-image/31mag-eat-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 771, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/31/magazine/31mag-eat-image/31mag-eat-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1542, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/31/magazine/31mag-eat-image/31mag-eat-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/31/magazine/31mag-eat-image/31mag-eat-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank'