8f'}, {'abstract': 'After years of ignoring and being ashamed of my hair, the coronavirus pandemic is forcing me to reassess our relationship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/27/opinion/coronavirus-hair-care.html', 'snippet': 'After years of ignoring and being ashamed of my hair, the coronavirus pandemic is forcing me to reassess our relationship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the first time in as long as I can remember, I miss the salon. Which isn’t to say that I miss the many minutes or sometimes hours spent waiting for the hairdresser to take you, even though you arrived for your appointment early; or the punishing heat of the dryer, which makes you hot behind the ears and sweaty at the nape of your neck; or the inevitable rough tug of the hairdresser and the urgent apology — Sorry! — as she combs through a stubborn tangle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27Phillips-slide-OL5J/27Phillips-slide-OL5J-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27Phillips-slide-OL5J/27Phillips-slide-OL5J-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27Phillips-slide-OL5J/27Phillips-slide-OL5J-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27Phillips-slide-OL5J/27Phillips-slide-OL5J-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27Phillips-slide-OL5J/27Phillips-slide-OL5J-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27Phillips-slide-OL5J/27Phillips-slide-OL5J-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27Phillips-slide-OL5J/27Phillips-slide-OL5J-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lockdown Taught Me to Care for My Natural Hair', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hair', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty Salons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-27T19:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maya Phillips', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Phillips', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/4049c912-0404-5372-a385-f6aa9b429c21', 'word_count': 1228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4049c912-0404-5372-a385-f6aa9b429c21'}, {'abstract': 'This is what it looks like when thousands of people die and there’s not enough room to store their bodies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/27/opinion/coronavirus-morgue-trucks-nyc.html', 'snippet': 'This is what it looks like when thousands of people die and there’s not enough room to store their bodies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was nearly two months ago when the first white refrigerated trucks began to appear on the streets of New York City. They were meant as a temporary solution to help overwhelmed hospitals and morgues house the bodies of people who had succumbed to Covid-19. The pandemic has now left nearly 30,000 dead in New York — and about 205 of the vehicles, sent by the Federal Emergency Management Agency or purchased by the medical examiner’s office, are stationed across the city.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27cher2/merlin_172852329_ea78a763-f992-472f-91df-6b066d7cf3dc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27cher2/merlin_172852329_ea78a763-f992-472f-91df-6b066d7cf3dc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27cher2/merlin_172852329_ea78a763-f992-472f-91df-6b066d7cf3dc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27cher2/merlin_172852329_ea78a763-f992-472f-91df-6b066d7cf3dc-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27cher2/merlin_172852329_ea78a763-f992-472f-91df-6b066d7cf3dc-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27cher2/merlin_172852329_ea78a763-f992-472f-91df-6b066d7cf3dc-thumbStandard.jpg