 organizational skills that the British prime minister himself knows he lacks and badly needs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Prime Minister Boris Johnson went to the mat yet again on Wednesday for his embattled adviser, Dominic Cummings, signaling to lawmakers that he had no plans to dismiss Mr. Cummings for breaching the rules by driving 260 miles to his parents’ house during the country’s coronavirus lockdown.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/world/27virus-britain/merlin_172886709_f78ae295-83fe-4cd6-a6cd-30ad6f79370b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/27/world/27virus-britain/merlin_172886709_f78ae295-83fe-4cd6-a6cd-30ad6f79370b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/world/27virus-britain/merlin_172886709_f78ae295-83fe-4cd6-a6cd-30ad6f79370b-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/world/27virus-britain/merlin_172886709_f78ae295-83fe-4cd6-a6cd-30ad6f79370b-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1473, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/world/27virus-britain/27virus-britain-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/27/world/27virus-britain/27virus-britain-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/world/27virus-britain/27virus-britain-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Boris Johnson Defends ‘Toxic’ Aide Again. Why Protect a Political Burden?', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'British Leader Defends ‘Toxic’ Aide Again, but Why Protect Political Burden?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Great Britain Withdrawal from EU (Brexit)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conservative Party (Great Britain)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Labour Party (Great Britain)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Yvette (1969- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cummings, Dominic (1971- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Boris', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-27T19:13:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler and Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/daf8cebb-6d44-57d3-8c14-d43b5bdcf10b', 'word_count': 1001, 'uri': 'nyt://article/daf8cebb-6d44-57d3-8c14-d43b5bdcf10b'}, {'abstract': 'Historically speaking, when white people are afraid, it is usually people of color who get hurt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/27/opinion/amy-cooper-central-park-racism.html', 'snippet': 'Historically speaking, when white people are afraid, it is usually people of color who get hurt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The symbolism is almost too much to bear. The antagonist stares down the barrel of the camera, removing her surgical face mask at the same moment she takes off her figurative mask and offers the audience a glimpse into what lies beneath. The woman, Amy Cooper, points her finger at the stranger behind the camera, Christian Cooper, to demand that he stop filming her. When he refuses, she threatens to call the police and then immediately acts on her threat.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27Hamad3/27Hamad3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 713, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27Hamad3/27Hamad3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 713}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27Hamad3/27Hamad3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 862, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27Hamad3/27Hamad3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1585, 'width': 1334, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27Hamad3/27Hamad3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27Hamad3/27Hamad3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27Hamad3/27Hamad3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A White Damsel Leveraged Racial Power and Failed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The White Damsel Goes Down', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whites', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery (Historical)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Amy (May 25, 2020 Central Park Incident)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Christian (Birder)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-27T19:15:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ruby Hamad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ruby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hamad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c13d954-c0da-526f-acc4-3906cdd860e7', 'word_count': 1044, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c13d954-c0da-526f-acc4-3906cdd860e7'}, {'abstract': 'The company, one of the few publicly traded nursing home operators, received $300 million in grants and loans, mostly from the federal government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/27/business/genesis-earnings-nursing-homes-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'The company, one of the few publicly traded nursing home operators, received $300 million in grants and loans, mostly from the federal government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The nation’s biggest nursing home operator, Genesis HealthCare, has received more than $300 million in government grants and loans to help it grapple with the coronavirus pandemic that has killed about 1,500 of its residents.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/business/27virus-markets-briefing-genesis/merlin_170025288_5559e9da-2348-44c9-8879-084e25189da4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/27/business/27virus-markets-briefing-genesis/merlin_170025288_5559e9da-2348-44c9-8879-084e25189da4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/business/27virus-markets-briefing-genesis/merlin_170025288_5559e9da-2348-44c9-8879-084e25189da4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/business/27virus-markets-briefing-genesis/merlin_170025288_5559e9da-2348-44c9-8879-084e25189da4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/business/27virus-markets-briefing-genesis/27virus-markets-briefing-genesis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/27/business/27virus-markets-briefing-genesis/27virus-markets-briefing-genesis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/business/27virus-markets-briefing-genesis/27virus-markets-briefing-genesis-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nursing Home Operator Genesis Details Coronavirus Aid', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nursing Home Giant Gets Over $300 Million in Aid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing Homes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Genesis Healthcare Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus Aid, Relief, and Economic Security Act (2020)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-27T19:18:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4138ff5d-d839-5717-a476-df1febd7b887', 'word_count': 1019, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4138ff5d-d839-5717-a476-df1febd7b887'}, {'abstract': 'Forget a V-shaped recovery, or even a U.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/27/opinion/coronavirus-economy-stimulus.html', 'snippet': 'Forget a V-shaped recovery, or even a U.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like dutiful soldiers, President Trump’s top economic advisers have been ardently echoing their boss’s optimism about the likelihood of a quick economic snapback, while downplaying the need for another rescue package.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27Rattner/27Rattner-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 424, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27Rattner/27Rattner-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 424}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27Rattner/27Rattner-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 724, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27Rattner/27Rattner-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1447, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27Rattner/27Rattner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27Rattner/27Rattner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27Rattner/27Rattner-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump’s Economic Advisers Are Wrong', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus Aid, Relief, and Economic Security Act (2020)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Powell, Jerome H', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mnuchin, Steven T', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-27T19:20:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Rattner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rattner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d3519fd-ce4c-56c7-96d9-123341d710ad', 'word_count': 857, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d3519fd-ce4c-56c7-96d9-123341d710ad'}, {'abstract': 'Social media and journalists alike amplify the president’s lies and propaganda.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/27/opinion/trump-twitter-ban.html', 'snippet': 'Social media and journalists alike amplify the president’s lies and propaganda.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every few months the same debate re-emerges: Should Twitter ban Donald Trump? Usually, it’s because of something particularly egregious, conspiratorial, untrue or geopolitically reckless that the president tweeted. Many of these tweets would result in a takedown or a temporary suspension if they came from a normal user’s account, but Twitter has made an exception for heads of state, citing a “newsworthiness” clause that allows the company to evade responsibility.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/opinion/27Warzel/27Warzel-articleLarge.j