 U.S. is back with more verve than a rocket’s red glare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAPE CANAVERAL, Fla. — For President Trump, it was a chance to rewrite the story line from tragedy to triumph. Even as the United States reached the grim milestone on Wednesday of 100,000 dead from the coronavirus pandemic, he would help mark the nation’s trailblazing return to human spaceflight from American soil.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/us/politics/27dc-trump/merlin_172892223_678f3ad3-c4c3-410f-b03a-e9b55ffc9ab9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/27/us/politics/27dc-trump/merlin_172892223_678f3ad3-c4c3-410f-b03a-e9b55ffc9ab9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/us/politics/27dc-trump/merlin_172892223_678f3ad3-c4c3-410f-b03a-e9b55ffc9ab9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 644, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/us/politics/27dc-trump/merlin_172892223_678f3ad3-c4c3-410f-b03a-e9b55ffc9ab9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1287, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/us/politics/27dc-trump/27dc-trump-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/27/us/politics/27dc-trump/27dc-trump-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/us/politics/27dc-trump/27dc-trump-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Cape Canaveral, Trump’s Search for a Heroic Narrative Is Thwarted', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trump’s Moment of Liftoff Fizzles in the Florida Rain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space and Astronomy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Space Exploration Technologies Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Spaceflight', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kennedy Space Center', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Musk, Elon', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cape Canaveral (Fla)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-27T20:15:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker and Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7ffad7c-f711-5f87-9369-cd67b341ccc7', 'word_count': 1348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7ffad7c-f711-5f87-9369-cd67b341ccc7'}, {'abstract': 'Tips for putting your best face forward, if only for an office staff meeting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/27/t-magazine/zoom-tips-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'Tips for putting your best face forward, if only for an office staff meeting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since the pandemic forced theaters to close their doors in mid-March, there has been no shortage of noble attempts to recreate the magic of the stage on streaming platforms including Zoom, Instagram Live and YouTube (where the Broadway interview show “Stars in the House” streams two theater productions daily). Virtual theater productions, of course, are mediated through technology and thus not experienced as they would be from the front mezzanine, and yet they’re not fully polished or always prerecorded, either. Part of the thrill of theater is its immediacy and, along with it, the potential for something to fall to pieces. That aspect remains perfectly intact, and recent performances have been felled by late starts, spotty internet and A/V connections, missed cues and poor lighting. “It can all feel like the local portions of the Jerry Lewis telethon,” jokes the producer and writer Jonathan Tolins. “As though these actors might be in their laundry rooms.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/t-magazine/27tmag-zoom/27tmag-zoom-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/27/t-magazine/27tmag-zoom/27tmag-zoom-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/27/t-magazine/27tmag-zoom/27tmag-zoom-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'