None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/cab1ba86-7c9c-5fab-97ac-255a31050133', 'word_count': 49, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cab1ba86-7c9c-5fab-97ac-255a31050133'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections that appeared in print on Thursday, May 28, 2020.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/27/pageoneplus/corrections-may-28-2020.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections that appeared in print on Thursday, May 28, 2020.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The full-page presentation on Sunday that listed the names of people whose lives were lost to the coronavirus pandemic included several errors. The list erroneously included Helyn Dawson because of a misreading of a local obituary. The list also misstated Sandra Piotrowski’s profession. She worked in the accounting departments of several manufacturing companies, not as a meat-cutter for Jewel supermarkets. The list misspelled the surname of a woman from Garrison, N.Y. She is Kerri Ann Kennedy-Tompkins, not Kennedy-Tomkins. The list misspelled the name of a woman from Philadelphia. She is Anibal Francisco de Brito; not Fracisco. It also misspelled the name of Jeffery Ronald Henry Muzljakovich’s hometown. It is Centerbrook, Conn., not Centerbook. It also misstated several ages: Chad Capule was 49, not 50. Vincent G. Frainee was 68, not 89. Ruth Hunter was 96, not 94, Benjamin Di Giovanni was 90, not 91. Shidao Wang was 72, not 75.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: May 28, 2020', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-05-28T03:28:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/662fa199-a32d-581e-8282-8bb2b412ed1b', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/662fa199-a32d-581e-8282-8bb2b412ed1b'}, {'abstract': 'In just the last week, even as some countries move to reopen, 700,000 new infections have been reported as the virus takes firmer hold in Latin America and the Middle East. The Boston Marathon has been canceled for 2020.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/28/world/coronavirus-live.html', 'snippet': 'In just the last week, even as some countries move to reopen, 700,000 new infections have been reported as the virus takes firmer hold in Latin America and the Middle East. The Boston Marathon has been canceled for 2020.', 'lead_paragraph': '新冠病毒疫情最新消息', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/28/world/28virus-int-briefing-brazil/28virus-int-briefing-brazil-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/28/world/28virus-int-briefing-brazil/28virus-int-briefing-brazil-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/28/world/28virus-int-briefing-brazil/28virus-int-briefing-brazil-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/28/world/28virus-int-briefing-brazil/28virus-int-briefing-brazil-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/28/world/28virus-int-briefing-brazil/28virus-int-briefing-brazil-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/28/world/28virus-int-briefing-brazil/28vi