lower — indoors versus everywhere else, the sounds of weather, memories pinging and humming.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Poem to create a space. Poem to invite us in, out of ourselves, into a new place of being. Poem that helps us gather the hay bales, pull them together. It’s a gift when a poem becomes its own little room so quickly. In David Watts’s “Pause,” from “Having and Keeping,” we keenly feel the sense of slower time that many of us have experienced in isolation — indoors versus everywhere else, the sounds of weather, memories of “the outer world” pinging and humming. Selected by Naomi Shihab Nye', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/31/magazine/31mag-poem-1/31mag-poem-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 292, 'width': 435, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/31/magazine/31mag-poem-1/31mag-poem-1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 292, 'width': 435, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/31/magazine/31mag-poem-1/31mag-poem-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/31/magazine/31mag-poem-1/31mag-poem-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/31/magazine/31mag-poem-1/31mag-poem-1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Poem: Pause', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-28T09:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Watts and Naomi Shihab Nye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Watts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Naomi', 'middlename': 'Shihab', 'lastname': 'Nye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c88e772c-92ea-54b0-ba97-ca605f81e0c1', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c88e772c-92ea-54b0-ba97-ca605f81e0c1'}, {'abstract': 'Experts identify common hazards in the home and what can be done to prevent accidents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/28/parenting/kids-home-safety.html', 'snippet': 'Experts identify common hazards in the home and what can be done to prevent accidents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As stay-at-home orders drag on and summer approaches, parents and caregivers will need to be more aware than ever of accident risks in the home. “More children spending more time staying at home and in the backyard means more needed supervision by parents who may be distracted by teleworking and caring for other family members,” said Joe Martyak, director of communications for the Consumer Product Safety Commission. “In this situation, kids’ exposure to risks goes up more than usual.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/28/multimedia/28virus-summer-safety/28virus-summer-safety-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/28/multimedia/28virus-summer-safety/28virus-summer-safety-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 