y The New York Times Opinion', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f350b151-930b-5ed0-b021-4b10f2c023f0', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f350b151-930b-5ed0-b021-4b10f2c023f0'}, {'abstract': 'My Zoom graduation felt like both a creepy, post-apocalyptic exercise and a corny, semi-pointless ritual.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/28/opinion/coronavirus-graduation-virtual-online-2020.html', 'snippet': 'My Zoom graduation felt like both a creepy, post-apocalyptic exercise and a corny, semi-pointless ritual.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Less than three months ago, I started having this uneasy feeling in the pit of my stomach. It started in early March when Harvard announced that it would finish the rest of its semester online. A few other schools quickly followed suit. At my school, Vassar College, the administration emailed us to say that we would be going online for a few weeks and returning to in-person classes in April.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/28/opinion/28Bretta/merlin_171946578_0529f965-fc41-408c-8dd6-971c00a8cf5e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/28/opinion/28Bretta/merlin_171946578_0529f965-fc41-408c-8dd6-971c00a8cf5e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/28/opinion/28Bretta/merlin_171946578_0529f965-fc41-408c-8dd6-971c00a8cf5e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/28/opinion/28Bretta/merlin_171946578_0529f965-fc41-408c-8dd6-971c00a8cf5e-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/28/opinion/28Bretta/28Bretta-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/28/opinion/28Bretta/28Bretta-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/28/opinion/28Bretta/28Bretta-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I Graduated Alone. In My Pajamas. On My Mom’s Couch.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I Graduated on My Mom’s Couch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commencement Speeches', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Videophones and Videoconferencing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Generation Z', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vassar College', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zoom Video Communications', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-28T19:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Retta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Retta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/34906587-efd3-577b-b92e-c6fe940e7f9f', 'word_count': 1289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34906587-efd3-577b-b92e-c6fe940e7f9f'}, {'abstract': 'Covid-19 deaths are being announced everywhere. Recognize the loss.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/28/opinion/coronavirus-social-media-death.html', 'snippet': 'Covid-19 deaths are being announced everywhere. Recognize the loss.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over 100,000 Americans have died from the coronavirus, and thanks to social media, many of us who aren’t personally in mourning are digitally connected to someone who is. Especially for people in the hardest-hit areas, death announcements in Facebook statuses, Instagram posts and tweets seem more frequent than they’ve ever been.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/28/opinion/28degroot/28degroot-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/28/opinion/28degroot/28degroot-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 720}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/28/opinion/28degroot/28degroot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 854, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/28/opinion/28degroot/28degroot-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1707, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/28/opinion/28degroot/28degroot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/28/opinion/28degroot/28degroot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbna