 {'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f9ea4fb-21f2-5c0a-8358-b6657af3559c', 'word_count': 1818, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f9ea4fb-21f2-5c0a-8358-b6657af3559c'}, {'abstract': 'What we wouldn’t give to spend an afternoon reading in the sun.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/29/books/review/dreaming-of-a-park-bench-and-a-book.html', 'snippet': 'What we wouldn’t give to spend an afternoon reading in the sun.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As summer approaches, we are longing for normalcy, a return to the sweaty June, July and August habits of our past lives in the city — things we maybe took for granted. The sound of an ice cream truck or the rumble of an air-conditioner perched precariously on a window ledge. Children screaming joyfully at a public pool. The block parties and sneaking wine into a concert in the park.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dreaming of a Park Bench and a Book', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-29T09:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gal Beckerman and Erica Ackerberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gal', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beckerman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ackerberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab6e3f9a-9dfa-5fa6-94fb-d5a96a422e6c', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab6e3f9a-9dfa-5fa6-94fb-d5a96a422e6c'}, {'abstract': 'The president’s indifference to collective grieving is of a piece with a political movement that denies our collective ties.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/29/opinion/coronovirus-mourning-trump.html', 'snippet': 'The president’s indifference to collective grieving is of a piece with a political movement that denies our collective ties.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than a hundred thousand lives have been lost to the Covid-19 pandemic in the United States, and while individuals and families have certainly grieved for their loved ones, there has been almost nothing in the way of a public remembrance of the lives lost. No national address; no moment of silence or official recognition beyond the occasional tweet and the flying of flags at half-staff over the Memorial Day weekend. No sense from the president or his subordinates that these were untimely deaths — needless losses that ought to occasion collective mourning. There will be no speech like President Barack Obama’s in the wake of the Mother Emanuel shooting in Charleston; no address like President Ronald Reagan’s after the Challenger disaster.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/01/opinion/1bouieprint/merlin_171914133_ed3d79f5-75db-4f81-9c71-11baf85e8ffd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/01/opinion/1bouieprint/merlin_171914133_ed3d79f5-75db-4f81-9c71-11baf85e8ffd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/01/opinion/1bouieprint/merlin_171914133_ed3d79f5-75db-4f81-9c71-11baf85e8ffd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo