763d01a1b'}, {'abstract': 'A document by prosecutors details how Mr. Chauvin, a former Minneapolis police officer, interacted with George Floyd before his death. Third-degree murder does not require an intent to kill.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/29/us/derek-chauvin-criminal-complaint.html', 'snippet': 'A document by prosecutors details how Mr. Chauvin, a former Minneapolis police officer, interacted with George Floyd before his death. Third-degree murder does not require an intent to kill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The former Minneapolis police officer charged in the death of George Floyd held his knee to Mr. Floyd’s neck for nearly nine minutes, including for two minutes and 53 seconds after Mr. Floyd became unresponsive, according to a document released by prosecutors on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/29/us/29minn-complaint-chauvin/29minn-complaint-chauvin-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 556, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/29/us/29minn-complaint-chauvin/29minn-complaint-chauvin-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 556}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/29/us/29minn-complaint-chauvin/29minn-complaint-chauvin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 948, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/29/us/29minn-complaint-chauvin/29minn-complaint-chauvin-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1897, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/29/us/29minn-complaint-chauvin/29minn-complaint-chauvin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/29/us/29minn-complaint-chauvin/29minn-complaint-chauvin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/29/us/29minn-complaint-chauvin/29minn-complaint-chauvin-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Derek Chauvin Was Charged With Third-Degree Murder', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Floyd, George (d 2020)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chauvin, Derek (1976- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minneapolis (Minn)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black Lives Matter Movement', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'George Floyd Protests (2020)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-30T00:13:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Mervosh and Nicholas Bogel-Burroughs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mervosh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bogel-Burroughs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1487068c-16ce-5bf7-95e6-9db693192229', 'word_count': 697, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1487068c-16ce-5bf7-95e6-9db693192229'}, {'abstract': 'The courts protected police abuses for years before George Floyd’s death. It’s time to rethink “qualified immunity.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/29/opinion/Minneapolis-police-George-Floyd.html', 'snippet': 'The courts protected police abuses for years before George Floyd’s death. It’s time to rethink “qualified immunity.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Minneapolis police officer, who was filmed kneeling on George Floyd’s neck for nearly nine minutes until the life left his body, has been fired, arrested and charged with third-degree murder and manslaughter. That is a step toward justice. Those who take a life should face a jury of their peers. But the rarity of the arrest, the fact that police officers who brutalize or even kill other people while wearing a badge so seldom end up facing any consequences is an ugly reminder of how unjust America’s legal system can be.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/30/opinion/30policeprint1/merlin_172907484_2f7cb8ad-dc3c-428b-910b-8e691bf0326b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/30/opinion/30policeprint1/merlin_172907484_2f7cb8ad-dc3c-428b-910b-8e691bf0326b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/30/opinion/30policeprint1/merlin_172907484_2f7cb8ad-dc3c-428b-910b-8e691bf0326b-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/30/opinion/30policeprint1/merlin_172907484_2f7cb8ad-dc3c-428b-910b-8e691bf0326b-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1386, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/30/opinion/30policeprint1/29policeWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/30/opinion/30policeprint1/29policeWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/30/opinion/30policeprint1/29policeWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How the Supreme Court Lets Cops Get Away With Murder', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Cops Get Away With Murder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Floyd, George (d 2020)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immunity from Prosecution', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'George Floyd Protests (2020)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black Lives Matter Movement', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-30T00:42:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ef6c781-ef8d-5265-890f-fb965acad69e', 'word_count': 1158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ef6c781-ef8d-5265-890f-fb965acad69e'}, {'abstract': 'The former national security adviser now says he does not remember those discussions as he fights a criminal charge he had previously pleaded guilty to.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/29/us/politics/flynn-russian-ambassador-transcripts.html', 'snippet': 'The former national security adviser now says he does not remember those discussions as he fights a criminal charge he had previously pleaded guilty to.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The former national security adviser Michael T. Flynn discussed sanctions at length with a Russian diplomat in late 2016, according to transcripts declassified on Friday that appear to bolster earlier assertions that Mr. Flynn misled Vice President Mike Pence and F.B.I. agents about those conversations.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/29/us/politics/29dc-flynn/merlin_172717452_6f7f1ffd-5d08-4f02-985d-6e0e08be28cd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/29/us/politics/29dc-flynn/merlin_172717452_6f7f1ffd-5d08-4f02-985d-6e0e08be28cd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/29/us/politics/29dc-flynn/merlin_172717452_6f7f1ffd-5d08-4f02-985d-6e0e08be28cd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/29/us/po