 but explaining the last few puzzles by Andrew J. Reis has taught me a lot, and I am finding myself increasingly prepared for his new puzzles. There are a few stumpers today, but if you’re getting to the point where you know your containers from your charades and your homophones, you might feel the same way about a clever little jewel box like this P and A. If not, then grab a guide and keep reading for hints — you’ll get there soon!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: Puns and Anagrams', 'kicker': 'SUNDAY VARIETY COLUMN', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-05-30T15:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Games', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caitlin Lovinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caitlin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a0230ad-9cab-5670-8b32-c0cc1b388649', 'word_count': 1118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a0230ad-9cab-5670-8b32-c0cc1b388649'}, {'abstract': 'Hand a kid colored pencils and the trepidation and confusion of the coronavirus pandemic transmutes into striped penguins.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/30/opinion/coronavirus-mcnaughton-art-children.html', 'snippet': 'Hand a kid colored pencils and the trepidation and confusion of the coronavirus pandemic transmutes into striped penguins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was a firefighter for many years. But because it was more than a decade ago, it often seems like another person wore those turnout boots, cinched that ax belt and ran into burning buildings. Yet when the Covid-19 pandemic hit a few months ago, my old first-responder instincts rose up.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/30/opinion/30paul1/30paul1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/05/30/opinion/30paul1/30paul1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/30/opinion/30paul1/30paul1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/30/opinion/30paul1/30paul1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1151, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/30/opinion/30paul1/30paul1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/05/30/opinion/30paul1/30paul1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/05/30/opinion/30paul1/30paul1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Case of Emergency, Make Art', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'MacNaughton, Wendy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-30T15:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caroline Paul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caroline', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Paul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd23df47-417c-52ff-8e7f-e2a9b90a769f', 'word_count': 1045, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd23df47-417c-52ff-8e7f-e2a9b90a769f'}, {'abstract': 'Estimates show the lockdown is pushing tens of millions of Indians below the poverty line.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/30/opinion/sunday/india-coronavirus-lockdown-inequality.html', 'snippet': 'Estimates show the lockdown is pushing tens of millions of Indians below the poverty line.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I landed in Delhi on a work trip in mid-March and just over a week later, Prime Minister Narendra Modi announced what was soon recognized as the world’s strictest lockdown. He warned Indians to imagine “a sacrosanct line” around their homes, not to be breached for work or travel of any kind, not even a walk outdoors. Evoking the 18-day war described in the Mahabharata, an ancient Indian epic, Mr. Modi said it would take 21 days to win the war on the coronavirus.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/01/opinion/sunday/01Sharma1/30Sharma1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/06/01/opinion/sunday/01Sharma1/30Sharma1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/06/01/opinion/sunday/01Sharma1/30Sharma1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'su