': 'Hygiene and Cleanliness', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marks, Matthew, Gallery (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Fork (NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gober, Robert', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-05-31T14:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deborah Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deborah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29145672-1690-5516-a92e-326e7e8bcf8c', 'word_count': 1279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29145672-1690-5516-a92e-326e7e8bcf8c'}, {'abstract': 'Making food is a way to make someone else’s life a little better, if only for a few minutes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/05/31/dining/what-to-cook-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'Making food is a way to make someone else’s life a little better, if only for a few minutes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. It seems ridiculous today, the nation roiled with anger, beset by fear and uncertainty, to tell you how nice it would be to make waffles, to eat in the fog still drifting past the window as the breakfast hour turns to brunch. It seems crazy to be recommending recipes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/09/14/dining/kc-tofu-katsu-horizontal/merlin_143375943_746f0b7a-6440-4a6e-96a1-e8b5a4827064-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/09/14/dining/kc-tofu-katsu-horizontal/merlin_143375943_746f0b7a-6440-4a6e-96a1-e8b5a4827064-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'